    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=970721": {
      "title": "Associate Professor in Chemical Processing for Batteries",
      "description": "Associate Professor in Chemical Processing for Batteries - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Associate Professor in Chemical Processing for Batteries 2026-10-07 Do you want to be part of an outstanding research environment within Ångström Advanced Battery Centre and move your research forward at Sweden’s largest faculty of science and technology? We are now looking for an associate professor who wishes to be involved in developing and strengthening our research and education in at the department of Chemistry at Ångström Laboratory. The Department of Chemistry – Ångström Laboratory has for many years hosted an environment focused on research and development of materials and their applications within the energy storage area: the Ångström Advanced Battery Centre. We develop novel electrode and electrolyte materials, characterize them, evaluate and improve them with respect to battery performance, and study fundamental chemical processes and properties using both experimental and computational techniques. The research is, as such, both fundamental and applied. The Department of Chemistry at Ångström conducts research and education in the chemistry field. The department has more than 270 employees and has a turnover of 300 million SEK. At the department's six programs, we conduct very successful research of a high international standard. We have a large number of externally funded research projects, often with international cooperation and we see continued good growth in our subject area. The department has education assignments in engineering programs and master's programs. More information is available on our website . Compel (Competence and excellence for the electrification of the transport system) is a strategic initiative from the Swedish government to ensure Sweden's long-term competitiveness in battery development and electrification of the transport sector. Research and education within the platform cover the entire battery value chain and offers an interdisciplinary network for collaboration between three universities: Lund University, Chalmers University of Technology and Uppsala University. It is within this context that Compel is now recruiting several young researchers with different competencies within the battery value chain, with the ambition to build a unique interdisciplinary research and education environment. This initiative is based on a strong partnership between academia and industry to drive research and development forward. Within the Compel initiative at Uppsala University, an associate professor will be employed at the Department of Chemistry at Ångström Laboratory to pursue research and education in the field of chemical processing for batteries. The new associate professor is invited to collaborate with the department's and Compel's researchers in an environment that supports the establishment of their own research group. The position comes with a starter package. Subject area The subject area of the position is chemical processing with a focus on experimental battery production, where Li-ion batteries are of prime interest. The broad scientific field includes, for example, chemical engineering, rheology, electrode engineering and battery cell production, and their correlation to battery performance. The research and teaching will include use of experimental infrastructure such as battery production lines. The field holds strong interconnections with battery materials production, utilization of batteries in devices such as electric vehicles or energy storage systems, and battery recycling. Duties : You will work with: Research: To establish an independent and internationally recognized research profile in chemical processing for batteries . To collaborate with research groups at the Department of Chemistry-Ångström Laboratory within the Faculty of Science and Technology. Actively applying for external grants. Teaching: This includes responsibility for courses, course administration and supervision of doctoral students. Administration: Participate in the general academic duties of Department of Chemistry-Ångström Laboratory. This includes serving on committees, taking on responsibilities beyond your own research and teaching assignments, contributing to the evaluation and development of teaching and research activities, working collaboratively with colleagues, and providing support and constructive feedback to colleagues. Keeping up to date in your subject area and following developments in society that are relevant to your work at Uppsala University. In choosing between eligible candidates, emphasis will primarily be given to both research and teaching expertise according weight to research expertise In addition, attention will be given to administrative, management, collaboration expertise. Qualifications required You must have: a PhD in Chemical Engineering or equivalent. research expertise in chemical processing for batteries such as chemical engineering, rheology, electrode engineering and battery cell production, including fabrication of commercial cell formats and sizes using relevant large-scale production technology. In addition to academic qualifications, research qualifications from other activities may also be taken into account, such as development of technology and capacity for innovation. teaching expertise, according particular weight to teaching in chemical enigneering. In addition to academic qualifications, educational and instructional qualifications from other activities may also be taken into account, such as supervision, internal training or mentoring programmes. completed at least ten weeks of teacher training for higher education of relevance to the organisation and its activities, or be considered to have acquired the equivalent knowledge. The required training for teachers in higher education may be completed during the first two years of employment if candidates lack it due to employment in industry or research institutes. a documented ability to teach in Swedish or English. an ability to work with other people and otherwise meet the demands of suitability required to perform the duties well. an ability to link research to teaching, based on the subject concerned, subject didactics and teaching and learning in higher education, and to interact on issues of teaching and learning in higher education with actors within and outside the University. research and teaching expertise or other professional expertise. The teaching expertise, research expertise and professional expertise must be relevant to the subject area and the duties that the position involves. Other desirable/valuable qualifications It is valuable if the applicant has: collaboration expertise. Interacting with the wider community, disseminating and exchanging information and translating research and development results into practical benefits. administrative expertise. Capacity to plan, organise and prioritise activities and to work in a structured manner that demonstrates an awareness of goals and quality. management expertise. Developing, coordinating and leading operations and staff. For more information on assessment and assessment criteria, see the Appointment Regulations for Uppsala University and the Faculty of Science and Technology’s Guidelines for the Appointement and Promotion of Teachers . All qualifications must be documented in a manner that makes it possible to assess both their quality and their scope. In this recruitment, the University will give primary consideration to the candidate who, following a qualitative overall assessment of their competence and expertise, is judged to have the best potential to perform and develop the relevant duties and to contribute to the positive development of the department/equivalent. Application Parental leave, part-time work due to childcare, trade union responsibilities, military service or similar activities are treated as work experience and should be listed in the CV. Instructions for applications for employment About the position: This is an open-ended appointment (a probationary period may apply). The position is full-time. Starting date 1st of March 2027 or as agreed. Place of work: Uppsala Further information about the position is available from: Prof. Daniel Brandell, +46-18-4713709, Daniel.Brandell@kemi.uu.se We look forward to receiving your application by November 16 2026, UFV-PA 2026/2777 . In the event of any disagreement between the English and the Swedish versions of this announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. We offer you Sweden offers good working conditions, including comprehensive social benefits such as generous family-focused policies that make healthcare, childcare, and children’s education available and highly affordable. At Uppsala University, we offer the opportunity for new international staff to learn Swedish through our language courses. If you have family, they will get new contacts and support through the Uppsala International Citizen hub. If you are an international candidate, you will find a lot of information about working and living in Sweden at http://www.uu.se/joinus. Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Department of Chemistry - Ångström Laboratory Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Permanent position – (starting with a temporary contract) Pay: Individuell Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/2777 Last application date: 16 November 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=971098": {
      "title": "Associate Professor in Computer Science specialising in Cybersecurity",
      "description": "Associate Professor in Computer Science specialising in Cybersecurity - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Associate Professor in Computer Science specialising in Cybersecurity 2026-10-07 We are now looking for an Associate Professor who will strengthen and complement the department's cybersecurity research environment through internationally visible and technically rigorous research. The research may cover foundational or applied aspects of cybersecurity. The successful candidate is expected to contribute to the long-term development of a leading international cybersecurity research environment. The Department of Information Technology holds a leading position in both research and education at all levels. We are currently Uppsala University's third largest department, have around 350 employees, including 100 teachers and 130 PhD students. Approximately 5,000 undergraduate students take one or more courses at the department each year. You can find more information about us on the Department of Information Technology website . Cybersecurity is the department’s newest research programme, established as part of strategic initiatives. The department conducts internationally recognized research across a broad range of cybersecurity areas, with particularly established strengths in software and web security and hardware security, as well as research activities in secure systems, network and information security, programming language security, trustworthy AI, federated learning, and cyber-physical security. The new Associate Professor will have the opportunity to establish their own research group in cybersecurity, strengthening growing research activities or initiating new directions complementary to well-established strengths in cybersecurity. The position has a generous starting package with additional research time during a limited period and funding for one PhD student. Subject area Cybersecurity is a broad area of computer science, with connections to several adjacent disciplines. It concerns the protection of information systems, and the data, services, and operations they support, against unauthorized access, manipulation, disclosure, and disruption. The subject encompasses research on the security of different layers and components of information and computing systems. Relevant research areas include, but are not limited to, systems and network security, malware and threat detection, software and application security, cryptography, hardware security, data security and privacy, and secure data processing and storage. Cybersecurity research also addresses security challenges and opportunities associated with evolving technologies and computing paradigms, including AI for cybersecurity, security and privacy of AI systems, cyber-physical systems, and IoT security. Human-centered aspects of cybersecurity are also within the subject area. Duties : You will work with: research. You will conduct foundational and technically rigorous cybersecurity research and contribute to the continued development of a leading international cybersecurity environment . The position offers the opportunity to help shape and strengthen a growing research team with active collaborations across computer science and related disciplines. Duties include publishing in leading international venues, supervising students and junior researchers, and actively applying for and obtain external research grants. teaching. Teaching includes responsibility for courses, course administration, and supervision of doctoral students. The position offers the opportunity to create new courses and participate in teacher teams involved in cybersecurity. administration. Participate in the general academic duties of the Department of Information Technology. This includes serving on committees, taking on responsibilities beyond your own research and teaching assignments, contributing to the evaluation and development of teaching and research activities, working collaboratively with colleagues, and providing support and constructive feedback to colleagues. keeping up to date in your subject area and following developments in society that are relevant to your work at Uppsala University. In choosing between eligible candidates, emphasis will primarily be given to both research and teaching expertise , which will be accorded equal weight. In addition, attention will be given to administrative, management and collaboration expertise. Qualifications required You must have: a PhD (within computer science or a similar field ). research expertise in cybersecurity, demonstrated through an internationally visible research profile of excellent scientific quality. In addition to academic qualifications, research qualifications from other activities may also be taken into account, such as development of technology and capacity for innovation. teaching expertise, according particular weight to experience with computer science courses . In addition to academic qualifications, educational and instructional qualifications from other activities may also be taken into account, such as supervision, internal training or mentoring programmes. completed at least ten weeks of teacher training for higher education of relevance to the organisation and its activities, or be considered to have acquired the equivalent knowledge. The required training for teachers in higher education may be completed during the first two years of employment if there are special reasons. a documented ability to teach in Swedish or English. an ability to work with other people and otherwise meet the demands of suitability required to perform the duties well. an ability to link research to teaching, based on the subject concerned, subject didactics and teaching and learning in higher education, and to interact on issues of teaching and learning in higher education with actors within and outside the University. a documented ability to obtain external grants in competition. demonstrated scientific impact. research and teaching expertise or other professional expertise. The teaching expertise, research expertise and professional expertise must be relevant to the subject area and the duties that the position involves. Other desirable/valuable qualifications It is valuable if the applicant has: research expertise in areas of cybersecurity that complement existing strengths and contribute to growing or new research directions with internationally visible research. Particular emphasis is placed on scientific quality and research contributions published in leading international venues in cybersecurity, such as ACM Conference on Computer and Communications Security, IEEE Symposium on Security and Privacy, USENIX Security Symposium, Network and Distributed System Security Symposium, or equivalent. teaching expertise, according particular weight to experience in cybersecurity courses. leadership roles within the international cybersecurity research community, including conference organization, program committee service, or editorial responsibilities. administrative experience in developing courses and curricula and running educational programmes. documented management expertise. Developing, coordinating and leading operations and staff. documented collaboration expertise. Interacting with the wider community, disseminating and exchanging information and translating research and development results into practical benefits. For more information on assessment and assessment criteria, see the Appointment Regulations for Uppsala University and the Faculty of Science and Technology’s Guidelines for the Appointement and Promotion of Teachers . All qualifications must be documented in a manner that makes it possible to assess both their quality and their scope. In this recruitment, the University will give primary consideration to the candidate who, following a qualitative overall assessment of their competence and expertise, is judged to have the best potential to perform and develop the relevant duties and to contribute to the positive development of the department/equivalent. Application Parental leave, part-time work due to childcare, trade union responsibilities, military service or similar activities are treated as work experience and should be listed in the CV. Instructions for applications for employment About the position: This is an open-ended appointment (a probationary period may apply). The position is full-time. Starting date 15 August 2027 or as agreed. Place of work: Uppsala Further information about the position is available from: Christian Rohner, +46 70-167 93 61, christian.rohner@it.uu.se and André Teixeira, +46 18 471 54 14, andre.teixeira@it.uu.se We look forward to receiving your application by 4 December 2026, UFV-PA 2026/2794. In the event of any disagreement between the English and the Swedish versions of this announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. Uppsala University’s tenure track career system entitles senior lecturers/associate professors to be considered for promotion to full professor. The University offers support for developing as a researcher and university teacher, leadership development, and patent and innovation support. We offer you Sweden offers good working conditions, including comprehensive social benefits such as generous family-focused policies that make healthcare, childcare, and children’s education available and highly affordable. At Uppsala University, we offer the opportunity for new international staff to learn Swedish through our language courses. If you have family, they will get new contacts and support through the Uppsala International Citizen hub . If you are an international candidate, you will find a lot of information about working and living in Sweden at http://www.uu.se/joinus. Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Disciplinary Domain of Science and Technology, Faculty of Mathematics and Computer Science, Department of Information Technology Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Permanent position Pay: Individually negotiated salary Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/2794 Last application date: 4 December 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
