    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=976320": {
      "title": "Research assistant",
      "description": "Research assistant - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Research assistant 2026-10-07 Research Assistant in Medical Cell Biology The Department of Medical Cell Biology at Uppsala University is a strong and international research environment. The department employs more than 110 staff members, including approximately 25 doctoral students, 10 postdoctoral researchers, and 40 researchers, lecturers, and professors. Description We are seeking a highly motivated Research Assistant to join our research group and contribute to projects related to pancreatic beta-cell biology. The successful candidate will support ongoing research into the molecular mechanisms underlying beta-cell function and dysfunction in diabetes.The work involves advanced cell culture models, molecular biology techniques, and high-content imaging. Duties The Research Assistant will be responsible for the following tasks: Cell Culture: Maintenance, cultivation, and experimental handling of pancreatic beta cells. Molecular Biology Analyses: Performing immunostaining, immunoblotting, RNA and DNA isolation, and PCR. High-Content Imaging: Conducting high-content imaging experiments and subsequent data analysis. Image and Data Analysis: Quantitative analysis of imaging data using ImageJ and CellProfiler. Documentation and Reporting: Accurate documentation of experiments and participation in scientific presentations. The position involves both independent work and collaboration with other researchers in an international research environment. Qualifications Applicants must have: A Master's degree in Molecular Medicine, Biomedicine, Cell Biology, or a related field. Documented hands-on experience in the cultivation of pancreatic beta cells. Documented experience with standard cell and molecular biology techniques, including: Immunostaining Immunoblotting RNA and DNA isolation PCR Cell imaging Good knowledge of image analysis using ImageJ and CellProfiler. Basic data analysis skills. Excellent written and spoken English skills. Additional Qualifications / Personal Attributes Great emphasis will be placed on personal suitability. We are looking for a candidate who demonstrates: Strong collaboration and interpersonal skills. Flexibility and adaptability. Attention to detail and a high degree of accuracy. A strong sense of responsibility. The ability to work both independently and as part of a team. Application Applications must be submitted through Uppsala University's recruitment system and should include: A cover letter describing your research experience and motivation for applying for the position. A Curriculum Vitae (CV), including information on relevant laboratory experience. Copies of degree certificates and academic transcripts. Contact details for at least two references, including their names, relationship to the applicant, and contact information. About the Position This is a fixed-term position of approximately 8 months, end date 2027-06-30. The position is full-time . Starting date by agreement. Location: Uppsala Further Information For further information about the position, please contact: Xuan Wang xuan.wang@mcb.uu.se Application Deadline Please submit your application no later than 21 October 2026 . Reference number: UFV-PA 2026/3004. Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Department of Medical Cell Biology Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Special fixed-term employment Pay: Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/3004 Last application date: 21 October 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=976831": {
      "title": "Kommunikatör till Centrum för kvinnors psykiska hälsa, WOMHER",
      "description": "Kommunikatör till Centrum för kvinnors psykiska hälsa, WOMHER - Uppsala University Use of cookies Uppsala University uses cookies to make your website experience better. Read more about cookies Accept all cookies Accept only necessary cookies Customize settings Skip to main content uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Kommunikatör till Centrum för kvinnors psykiska hälsa, WOMHER Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Kommunikatör till Centrum för kvinnors psykiska hälsa, WOMHER This job advertisement is only available in Swedish . HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
