    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=972169": {
      "title": "PhD in psychology",
      "description": "PhD in psychology - Uppsala University Use of cookies Uppsala University uses cookies to make your website experience better. Read more about cookies Accept all cookies Accept only necessary cookies Customize settings Skip to main content uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies PhD in psychology Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation PhD in psychology 2026-10-01 PhD student in developmental psychology Are you interested in working with developmental psychology, with the support of competent and friendly colleagues in an international environment? Are you looking for an employer that invests in sustainable employeeship and offers safe, favourable working conditions? We welcome you to apply for a fully funded PhD position at Uppsala University. Within the Development and Neurodiversity Lab (DiVE), we study early childhood development. One of our projects is a unique longitudinal twin study of young children, in which we investigate how genetic and environmental factors contribute to individual differences in brain development and behavior. The PhD student will work within this study, focusing on the development of temperament, emotion regulation, and prosocial behavior. Data collection for the study has been completed, and the cohort comprises more than 1,000 twins (500 twin pairs). Duties The duties primarily involve formulating research questions, analyzing data, writing scientific articles, and presenting research findings orally in a variety of contexts. In addition to research work, the doctoral program includes coursework equivalent to 60 higher education credits. The duties may also include teaching and other departmental responsibilities, up to a maximum of 20% of full working time. Eligible for admission to the PhD-program is anyone who meets the university´s conditions for both the general and the specific entry requirements. Eligibility also requires that the applicant is considered to have the capabilities needed to complete the education. (cf. SFS 2010:1064, HF ch. 7 § 35). The general entry requirements are met by those who have completed a degree at advanced level, completed course requirements of at least 240 higher education credits, of which at least 60 higher education credits are at advanced level. The general entry requirements are also met by those who have acquired essentially equivalent knowledge in some other way within or outside of Sweden. The university may, for an individual applicant, grant exemptions from the general requirements if there are special reasons. (cf. SFS 2010:1064, HF ch. 7 § 39). The specific entry requirements are met by those who have passed psychology courses of 90 credits. The specific entry requirements are also met by those who have acquired essentially equivalent knowledge in some other way within or outside of Sweden. Specific requirements Excellent proficiency in spoken and written English is required, as well as strong general communication and collaboration skills. The position also requires documented experience in, and aptitude for, quantitative data analysis and statistics. Desirable qualifications Experience with research similar to that conducted within the group. Documented experience of taking independent responsibility for projects and driving them forward under supervision. Programming skills. More information about PhD studies in psychology: https://www.uu.se/en/department/psychology/study/phd-studies Rules governing PhD students are set out in the Higher Education Ordinance chapter 5, §§ 1-7. Application procedure The application must be written in Swedish or English and contain as follow: Application for admission A personal statement, no longer than one A4 page, in which you specifically comment on your suitability in relation to the specific requirements and desired qualifications listed above, as well as any other information that is directly relevant Curriculum vitae (CV) Certified diploma confirming that you have basic and special qualifications Register extract of completed relevant courses Contact details for clinical and academic references Other meritorious information, for example publications Description of the assessment procedure for the PhD program in psychology. About the employment The employment is a temporary position according to the Higher Education Ordinance chapter 5 § 7 . Scope of employment 100 %. Starting February 1, 2027 or as agreed. Placement: Uppsala For further information about the position, please contact: Professor Terje Falck-Ytter, terje.falck-ytter@psyk.uu.se Please submit your application by November 2, 2026. UFV-PA 2026/2915. Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Department of Psychology Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Temporary position Pay: Fast lön Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/2915 Last application date: 2 November 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
