    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=973784": {
      "title": "Two PhD students in Chemistry with specialisation in Organic Chemistry",
      "description": "Two PhD students in Chemistry with specialisation in Organic Chemistry - Uppsala University Use of cookies Uppsala University uses cookies to make your website experience better. Read more about cookies Accept all cookies Accept only necessary cookies Customize settings Skip to main content uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Two PhD students in Chemistry with specialisation in Organic ... Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Two PhD students in Chemistry with specialisation in Organic Chemistry 2026-09-30 Two PhD students in Chemistry with specialisation in Organic Chemistry The Department of Chemistry for Life Sciences conducts research and education in analytical chemistry, biochemistry, and organic chemistry. More than 100 people, including around 45 PhD students, work at the department. New employees and students are recruited from all over the world and English is the main working language. The department is located at the Biomedical Centre in Uppsala, which facilitates collaborations with research groups in biology, pharmacy, medicine and SciLifeLab and gives access to advanced infrastructure for experimental and theoretical studies. The international environment and good opportunities for interdisciplinary collaborations enables PhD students at the department to participate in relevant research projects and prepare for an international research career. Read more about the research at The Department of Chemistry for Life Sciences at our website . Project description The PhD student will participate in an innovative project involving elements from supramolecular chemistry, molecular recognition, catalysis and chemistry of heavier main-group elements, aiming at discovery of novel routes for selective synthesis. Key analytical techniques to be used include advanced multinuclear NMR as well as other advanced methods for studying molecular structure and molecular interactions. Duties The main duties of PhD students are to devote themselves to their research studies, which includes participating in research projects and third cycle courses. The work duties can also include teaching and other departmental duties (not more than 20 % of full time). Read more about being a Doctoral student here . Requirements To be eligible for doctoral education, a basic higher education equivalent to at least 240 ECTS credits, including at least 60 ECTS credits at Master’s level, including an independent project equivalent to at least 15 credits, or has acquired substantially equivalent knowledge in some other way, is required. More information about the general requirements can be found here . A student has special eligibility for doctoral studies in organic chemistry if s/he has passed courses of at least 90 higher education credits (or equivalent) of courses relevant to the specialization. At least 40 higher education credits must be in organic chemistry at an advanced level (second cycle). More information about the subject specific requirements can be found here . Emphasis will also be placed on personal qualities such as good collaborative skills, motivation, and independence, as well as how the applicant through his/her experience and competence is judged to have the abilities necessary to develop within and acquire the doctoral education. Good English communication, including an ability to clearly disseminate research findings orally and in writing, are essential. Additional qualifications Selection will be based on the applicant’s educational background (BSc as well as MSc level with emphasis on the latter), relevant practical and communication skills and additional experiences relevant for successfully undertaking the PhD education and the project. A background in experimental organic synthesis, the development or investigation of catalytic processes, or the study of non-covalent interactions will be considered favourably. Familiarity with analytical and characterisation techniques such as NMR and UV–Vis spectroscopy, mass spectrometry, X-ray crystallography, and chromatographic methods for purification and analysis would also be advantageous. Relevant experiences, knowledge and skills should be clearly documented in the application and may be exemplified by content and result from taught courses, degree projects, research placements and employments as well as reports, including any publication in international peer-reviewed journals. Doctoral students normally participate for some in teaching at undergraduate and graduate levels. Previous experience from teaching/mentoring, also from environments outside of school/university, as well as other outreach activities may therefore be an advantage. Rules governing PhD students are set out in the Higher Education Ordinance chapter 5, §§ 1-7 and in Uppsala University's rules and guidelines. About the employment The employment is a temporary position according to the Higher Education Ordinance chapter 5 § 7 . Scope of employment 100%. The intended starting date is 14th January 2027 or as agreed upon. Placement: Uppsala For further information about the position, please contact: (e-mail: andrew.docker@kemi.uu.se) Please submit your application by 29 October 2026, UFV-PA 2026/2895. Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Department of Chemistry - BMC Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Temporary position Pay: Doktorandstege Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/2895 Last application date: 29 October 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=974072": {
      "title": "PhD student position in Bioinformatics/Evolutionary Microbiology",
      "description": "PhD student position in Bioinformatics/Evolutionary Microbiology - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation PhD student position in Bioinformatics/Evolutionary Microbiology 2026-09-30 The Department of Medical Biochemistry and Microbiology (IMBIM) at Uppsala University provides a broad international environment for research and teaching. Research at IMBIM spans biochemistry, molecular and cell biology, structural biology, tumour biology, comparative genetics, functional genomics, immunology, bacteriology and virology. The research has a basic-science orientation, with strong relevance to mechanisms of health and disease in both animals and humans. More info: Research – Department of Medical Biochemistry and Microbiology – Uppsala University We are looking for a highly motivated PhD student to join the project “A two-billion-year history of infections: evolution of host-adaptation in early Gammaproteobacteria”, funded by the Swedish Research Council and led by Lionel Guy. The PhD student will be located at the Biomedical Centre, Uppsala, Sweden. Project description The ability to feed on other organisms through phagocytosis is a crucial step in the evolution of eukaryotes, a prerequisite for food webs, multicellularity and probably the acquisition of mitochondria. It also paved the way for intracellular parasitism, as some bacteria avoided digestion by their hosts and multiplied in the nutrient-rich cytoplasm. Here, we focus on the Deep-branching Intracellular Gammaproteobacteria (DIG), a large group of related bacteria (e.g. Legionella and Francisella ) with a wide variety of host-adaptation strategies. We hypothesize that the last common ancestor of DIG appeared during eukaryogenesis, 2 billion years ago, and was among the first bacteria to infect eukaryotes. In this project, the PhD student will gather a solid set of DIG genomes, including isolates belonging to 30 novel species of Legionella , reconstruct their evolutionary history, assess their metabolic potential, and identify their host-adaptation genes. They will screen genomes for horizontal gene transfers from early eukaryotes or Asgard archaea and specifically analyse the evolution of the Legionella genus. A better understanding of the relationships between the first eukaryotes and their early invaders will shed light on eukaryogenesis, and particularly on the role of phagocytosis. Required Qualifications To meet the entry requirements for doctoral studies, you must hold a Master’s (second-cycle) degree in bioinformatics, molecular biology, microbiology, microbial ecology or a similar field or have completed at least 240 credits in higher education, with at least 60 credits at Master’s level including an independent project worth at least 15 credits, or have acquired substantially equivalent knowledge in some other way. The degree should be completed, or expected to be completed, before March 2027. Documented coding skills in Python or R Experience in using and/or developing methods in metagenomics and molecular evolution Background understanding of, and interest in, microbial evolution Proficiency in spoken and written English Ability to plan, carry out and complete research projects independently Creativity and good teamwork skills Desirable qualifications Experience of building pipelines for high-performance computing (HPC) clusters Competence in handling large datasets Experience with DNA extraction and sequencing library preparation The selection is based on the following criteria: completion of the above qualifications, grades in relevant courses, the relevance of those courses to the research programme, and previous experience of work and research in the wider area of the project described above. An overall assessment of the applicant will be made in order to employ the best possible candidate, who can succeed in the doctoral studies and contribute to a positive development of the research programme. Emphasis will be placed on personal qualities, including analytical ability, accuracy, flexibility and collaborative skills. Rules governing PhD students are set out in the Higher Education Ordinance chapter 5, §§ 1-7 and in Uppsala University's rules and guidelines . About the employment The employment is a temporary position according to the Higher Education Ordinance chapter 5 § 7 . Scope of employment 100 %. Starting date as soon as possible or as agreed. Placement: Uppsala For further details , please contact Associate Professor Lionel Guy, lionel.guy@imbim.uu.se Application: Please submit your application through the Uppsala University application portal, including a CV, a letter describing your research interests and skills, publications or a copy of your Master’s thesis or equivalent, and contact details for two referees (telephone number and e-mail address). Please submit your application by 29 October 2026, UFV-PA 2026/2912. Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Department of Medical Biochemistry and Microbiology Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Temporary position Pay: Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/2912 Last application date: 29 October 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=974523": {
      "title": "PhD student in Media and Communication Studies",
      "description": "PhD student in Media and Communication Studies - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation PhD student in Media and Communication Studies 2026-09-30 Are you interested in working with research in Media and Communication, with the support of competent and friendly colleagues in an international environment? Are you looking for an employer that invests in sustainable employeeship and offers safe, favourable working conditions? We welcome you to apply for a position as PhD student in Media and communication studies at Uppsala University. The Department of Informatics and Media has a broad research profile grounded in contemporary research fields, including information systems, interaction design, and media and communication. Within the discipline of Media and Communication Studies , research focuses on various forms of communication and media in both global and local contexts. The work within the research environment is connected through a deeply interdisciplinary and critical approach, employing both qualitative and quantitative methods. We study media and communication as fundamental to understanding contemporary social change as well as to defining the conditions and challenges of human coexistence. Duties The position is a fully funded doctoral studentship in Media and Communication Studies at the Department of Informatics and Media. Doctoral education comprises four years of full-time study. The doctoral candidate is expected to devote the main part of their working time to doctoral education (see project description below) and to actively participate in the department’s seminar activities, workshops, conferences, and similar events. Other duties, such as teaching and research administration – in English and/or Swedish – may also be included as part of the employment (up to a maximum of 20%). The doctoral student will join the project AI Confidential: Emerging Forms of AI Chatbot Use for Emotional Support and Personal Well-being Among Young Swedes , funded by the Swedish Research Council (Grant No. 2026-00497). The project explores how young people (aged 15–18) interpret and relate to AI as a conversational partner in personal areas of life, as well as the opportunities and challenges that traditional healthcare providers experience in relation to this development. The doctoral student is expected to plan and conduct empirical studies within the project, drawing on an existing collaboration with the Youth Guidance Centres in Sweden’s Västmanland Region and working in close collaboration with the research team. The project is led by Matilda Tudor (PI), Media and Communication Studies, and Lina Eklund (co-PI), Human-Computer Interaction; both have research profiles in critical digital media studies and everyday automation. Read more about the project here. Requirements To meet the entry requirements for doctoral studies, you must hold a Master’s (second-cycle) degree in Media and Communication Studies or a closely related/equivalent field, or have completed at least 240 credits in higher education, with at least 90 credits at Master’s level including an independent project worth at least 15 credits, within Media and Communication Studies or a closely related/equivalent field, or have acquired substantially equivalent knowledge in some other way. We are looking for a candidate with a strong interest in young people’s living conditions and new technologies. The candidate should have documented experience of working with research-related tasks in Media and Communication Studies, for example through having completed a Master’s-level thesis. The candidate should have documented experience of working with interview methods and/or surveys, and must be able to conduct qualitative research interviews in Swedish. Fluency in Swedish is therefore required, as well as excellent proficiency in spoken and written English. Great importance will be placed on the candidate’s personal suitability for the position and interest in the subject area. In addition to academic qualifications, important qualifications include the ability to collaborate, initiative, independence, and a critical, reflective, and analytical approach. Personal skills should also be substantiated through documentation. When the University appoints new doctoral students, applicants will be selected who, following a qualitative overall assessment of their competence and qualifications, are judged to have the best conditions for carrying out and developing the tasks in question, particularly within the doctoral project, and for contributing to the positive development of activities within the field. Qualifications and merits must be documented in such a way that both their quality and scope can be assessed. Interviews will be conducted either in person or digitally at Uppsala University. Regulations concerning doctoral students are set out in Chapter 5, Sections 1–7 of the Swedish Higher Education Ordinance (Högskoleförordningen), as well as in the University’s rules and guidelines. The application must include: A brief cover letter , which should contain:1) The applicant’s motivation for applying for the position (maximum 500 words). 2) A brief description of the documents submitted (list them). 3) If more than one academic work (thesis, article, etc.) is submitted for assessment, the cover letter must specify which of these the admissions committee should prioritize. Doctoral project plan (maximum two pages, in English). The plan should include the theoretical framework, research questions, aims, type of data, methodology, and timeline. CV with certified copies of academic documents , such as transcripts, demonstrating that the applicant meets the eligibility requirements for doctoral studies in Media and Communication Studies, as well as copies of certified degree certificates and grades. Two letters of recommendation. Copies of independent academic works authored by the applicant as part of their undergraduate or graduate education (C-, D-, or advanced level, or equivalent; drafts of ongoing work may be attached), or other relevant texts. Any other documents the applicant wishes to include. PLEASE NOTE: Incomplete applications will not be considered. About the employment The employment is a temporary position according to the Higher Education Ordinance chapter 5 § 7. Scope of employment 100 %. Starting date 1 january or as agreed. Placement: Uppsala For further information about the position, please contact: Project leadar - Matilda Tudor, matilda.tudor@im.uu.se Head of Department – Tomas Eklund, tomas.eklund@im.uu.se Chair of Media and Communication Studies - Michał Krzyżanowski, michal.krzyzanowski@im.uu.se Please submit your application by 13 November 2026, UFV-PA 2026/2934 Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Department of Informatics and Media Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Temporary position Pay: Enligt avtal Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/2934 Last application date: 13 November 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=971008": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Offshore Renewable Energy with Specialisation in Computational Methods",
      "description": "Assistant Professor in Offshore Renewable Energy with Specialisation in Computational Methods  - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Assistant Professor in Offshore Renewable Energy with Specialisation in Computational Methods 2026-09-29 Do you want to be part of a leading research environment in renewable energy and advance your research at Sweden's largest Faculty of Science and Technology? We are now recruiting an Assistant Professor who will contribute to the development of research and education in offshore renewable energy. The Department of Electrical Engineering conducts multidisciplinary research across the full spectrum of electrical engineering, from technologies for renewable electricity generation and the electrification of the transport sector to 5G/6G communications and smart electrical sensors. The successful candidate will join the Division of Electricity, an international and interdisciplinary research environment with strong expertise in computational science, energy systems, fluid mechanics, and the sustainable energy transition. Research is carried out in close collaboration with national and international universities, research institutes, and industrial partners. The division provides access to advanced high-performance computing infrastructure as well as experimental and numerical facilities supporting research on next-generation offshore energy systems. More information about the Department of Electrical Engineering is available at: https://www.uu.se/en/department/electrical-engineering Subject Area We seek an outstanding early-career researcher who wishes to develop research and education in advanced numerical methods for modelling and simulation of complex physical processes associated with offshore energy systems. The successful candidate is expected to establish an independent and internationally competitive research programme focusing on numerical modelling of fluid–structure interaction and the development of computational tools for next-generation renewable energy technologies. The research should contribute to robust, efficient, and sustainable solutions for floating offshore wind, wave energy, and other marine renewable energy systems. Duties You will work with: Conduct research of the highest international quality. This includes developing and leading an independent research group, collaborating with researchers within the department as well as with international research groups and industry, and contributing to the strategic development of the department and the university. The position also includes actively seeking and securing external research funding. Teaching. Teaching responsibilities include course coordination, course administration, and supervision of undergraduate, master's and PhD students. The successful candidate is also expected to contribute to the development of courses in renewable energy engineering. Participate in departmental administration and contribute to the general academic responsibilities of the Department of Electrical Engineering. This includes serving on committees, taking on responsibilities beyond one's own research and teaching, participating in the evaluation and development of educational and research activities, collaborating with colleagues, and contributing to a constructive academic environment. Maintain up-to-date expertise within the subject area and follow developments in society that are relevant to the position at Uppsala University. Among qualified applicants, selection will be based primarily on scientific and pedagogical excellence, with particular emphasis placed on scientific merits. The ability to secure external research funding, collaborate effectively with external stakeholders, and demonstrate leadership potential will also be considered. Qualifications required You must have: A PhD in a field relevant to the position, such as engineering mechanics, energy systems, fluid mechanics, or a related discipline. Priority will be given to applicants who obtained their doctoral degree, or achieved equivalent competence, no more than seven years before the closing date for applications. Demonstrated scientific excellence in offshore renewable energy, including research relevant to wave energy, floating offshore wind, and related marine renewable energy technologies. Applicants should have documented expertise in one or more of the following areas: fluid mechanics, numerical methods, high-performance computing, optimisation, and the design of complex energy systems. Scientific excellence must be demonstrated through publications in leading international peer-reviewed journals. Demonstrated teaching expertise, with particular emphasis on experience in theoretical, numerical, and experimental education. The ability to integrate research, subject-specific pedagogy, and higher education pedagogy into teaching is considered essential. Completed higher education teaching training equivalent to at least five weeks, or possess equivalent documented competence. If special circumstances apply, such training may be completed during the first two years of employment. Documented ability to teach in Swedish or English. Demonstrated ability to collaborate effectively and otherwise meet the personal suitability requirements necessary to perform the duties of the position. A documented ability to obtain external research funding in competitive calls. Particular merit will be given to prestigious national or European research grants. Scientific and pedagogical expertise relevant to the subject area and duties of the position. Other desirable/valuable qualifications It would be an advantage if you have: Experience in the development and application of scientific software or numerical methods for offshore renewable energy systems, including physics-based modelling as well as emerging data-driven and AI-enabled approaches. Experience in high-performance scientific computing of offshore renewable energy systems, including advanced CFD-simulations. Experience of industrial research collaborations relevant to the position. International research collaborations and a strong international research network. For more information on assessment and assessment criteria, see the Appointment Regulations for Uppsala University and the Faculty of Science and Technology’s Guidelines for the Appointement and Promotion of Teachers . All qualifications must be documented in a manner that makes it possible to assess both their quality and their scope. When the University appoints new academic staff, candidates will be selected based on a qualitative overall assessment of their competence and expertise, taking into account their potential to perform and develop the duties of the position and to contribute to the positive development of the department. Application Parental leave, part-time work due to childcare, trade union responsibilities, military service or similar activities are treated as work experience and should be listed in the CV. Instructions for applications for employment Period of employment The position of Assistant Professor is fixed-term for up to six years and is intended to provide qualifications for a permanent teaching position with higher eligibility requirements. During the appointment, there is the possibility to apply for promotion to Associate Professor. If the requirements are met and suitability is confirmed, the appointee may be promoted to a permanent position as Associate Professor. About the position This is a temporary full-time position six years. The position is full-time (100%). Starting date 1 March or as agreed. Place of work: Uppsala, Sweden Further information about the position is available from: Karin Thomas, 018-471 3098, karin.thomas@uu.se We look forward to receiving your application by 12 November, UFV-PA 2026/2787 In the event of any disagreement between the English and the Swedish versions of this announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. We offer you Sweden offers good working conditions, including comprehensive social benefits such as generous family-focused policies that make healthcare, childcare, and children’s education available and highly affordable. At Uppsala University, we offer the opportunity for new international staff to learn Swedish through our language courses. If you have family, they will get new contacts and support through the Uppsala International Citizen hub . If you are an international candidate, you will find a lot of information about working and living in Sweden at http://www.uu.se/joinus . Uppsala University’s tenure track system grants assistant professors the possibility to be assessed for promotion to the position as associate professor. The university provides support in various areas, such as scientific and educational development, leadership development as well as patent and innovation support. Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Disciplinary Domain of Science and Technology, Faculty of Technology, Department of Electrical Engineering Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Temporary position Pay: Individually negotiated salary Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/2787 Last application date: 12 November 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=971449": {
      "title": "PhD position in patient preference research in amputation, prosthetics and rehabilitation",
      "description": "PhD position in patient preference research in amputation, prosthetics and rehabilitation - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation PhD position in patient preference research in amputation, prosthetics and rehabilitation 2026-09-29 The Centre for Research Ethics and Bioethics (CRB) is an interdisciplinary centre located at the Department of Public Health and Caring Sciences at Uppsala University. The centre’s researchers hold degrees in medicine, healthcare, ethics, philosophy, and law, and examine the ethical, philosophical, and legal aspects of biomedical research and clinical practice. Duties We are seeking a PhD candidate to empirically investigate patients’ experiences, preferences, and perceptions of what constitutes high-value rehabilitation following amputation. The PhD candidate will primarily conduct international preference studies using the Discrete Choice Experiment (DCE) methodology to examine how patients value different aspects of rehabilitation, such as access to care, waiting times, prosthetic device characteristics, independence, social participation, and quality of life, and how these preferences may vary across patient groups and healthcare systems. This is an interdisciplinary EU-funded project, named ThRIVE, in which the PhD candidate will join an international research team with expertise in ethics, rehabilitation, prosthetics and orthotics, biomechanics, health economics, and preference research. The project is closely integrated with international research networks and offers opportunities to build a strong international academic network. The work will include data wrangling and statistical analyses in RStudio, as well as developing DCE designs using tools such as Ngene and Sawtooth. The project is based at the Centre for Research Ethics & Bioethics (CRB) in the Department of Public Health and Caring Sciences at Uppsala University. Read more about the project here: major-international-project-aims-to-improve-conditions-for-amputees Requirements Applicants must hold a Master’s (second-cycle) degree in prosthetics and orthotics, physiotherapy, occupational therapy, health sciences, public health, health economics, or another discipline relevant to the project, or have completed at least 240 credits in higher education, with at least 60 credits at Master’s level, including an independent project worth at least 15 credits in one of the above disciplines or another relevant field, or have acquired substantially equivalent knowledge in some other way. Proficiency in English, both spoken and written, is required. Read more about doctoral education, entry requirements, and admission regulations here: Doctoral studies – Disciplinary Domain of Medicine and Pharmacy – Staff – Uppsala University Additional qualifications We welcome applicants who either have a background in prosthetics and rehabilitation and are interested in developing expertise in Discrete Choice Experiment (DCE) methodology, or who have experience in DCEs and preference research and wish to deepen their knowledge of amputation, prosthetic provision, and rehabilitation. We are looking for a motivated and independent individual who can take initiative, solve problems, and work in a structured and quality-conscious manner. Experience with RStudio is considered an advantage. The PhD candidate will work in a multidisciplinary environment in which individuals with diverse backgrounds, qualifications, and areas of expertise collaborate to conduct innovative research. Rules governing PhD students are set out in the Higher Education Ordinance chapter 5, §§ 1-7 and in Uppsala University's rules and guidelines. Application: Your application should include a cover letter, CV, copies of degree certificates and academic transcripts, your thesis/project work, and any previous publications (e.g., Bachelor’s or Master’s thesis). In your cover letter, please describe: (1) your experience of conducting scientific research, (2) your motivation for pursuing doctoral studies, (3) your experience with the statistical software RStudio, and (4) your background in prosthetics and rehabilitation and/or your experience with preference research and Discrete Choice Experiments (DCEs). Please also explain how your previous experiences could contribute to the project and how you would like to further develop and shape the PhD project beyond the DCE study described. Selection Process: Applicants will be selected based on the following criteria: fulfilment of the qualification and eligibility requirements, as well as previous experience in work and/or research within related fields. The selection of applicants is carried out by the supervisors in consultation with the department's doctoral education committee. The doctoral candidate is formally admitted by the Faculty's Committee for Doctoral Education. In this recruitment process, the University will primarily consider the applicant who, following an overall assessment of qualifications and competencies, is deemed to have the best potential to successfully carry out and further develop the duties associated with the position. About the employment The employment is a temporary position according to the Higher Education Ordinance chapter 5 § 7 . Scope of employment 100%. Starting date 2027-01-01 or as agreed. Placement: Uppsala. For further information about the position, please contact: Jennifer Viberg Johansson, +46 18 471 62 81, jennifer.viberg-johansson@uu.se Please submit your application by 21 October 2026 , UFV-PA 2026 /2802. Are you considering moving to Sweden to work at Uppsala University? Find out more about what it´s like to work and live in Sweden. Why you should come and work in Sweden – Uppsala University Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Disciplinary Domain of Medicine and Pharmacy, Faculty of Medicine, Department of Public Health and Caring Sciences Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Temporary position Pay: Fixed salary Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/2802 Last application date: 21 October 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=973887": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral position in Practically Usable Verification for Numerical Programs",
      "description": "Postdoctoral position in Practically Usable Verification for Numerical Programs - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Postdoctoral position in Practically Usable Verification for Numerical Programs 2026-09-29 Are you interested in working in automated program verification with the support of competent and friendly colleagues in an international environment? Are you looking for an employer that invests in sustainable employeeship and offers safe, favorable working conditions? We welcome you to apply for a postdoctoral position at the Department of Information Technology at Uppsala University. The Department of Information Technology holds a leading position in both research and education at all levels. We are currently Uppsala University's third largest department, and have around 350 employees, including 120 teachers and 120 PhD students. Approximately 5,000 undergraduate students take one or more courses at the department each year. You can find more information about us on the Department of Information Technology website . The postdoctoral position is hosted by the Division of Computing Science and specifically within the Programming Languages group that currently consists of 11 senior researchers and 10 PhD students that are working on different aspects of programming language design, program verification and software engineering. Beyond technical collaborations, the group meets regularly and provides an engaging and supportive environment. Project description and duties The available postdoctoral position is within a project that aims to make it easier for developers to write correct and efficient numerical programs. The project will include both a theoretical part, developing new techniques and approaches, as well as implementations that can be practically used. The project targets specifically numerical programs that appear widely in e.g. safety-critical (embedded) systems, data analysis, weather forecasting, physics, and engineering. Verifying that such programs are correct is challenging because of rounding errors due to floating-point arithmetic. Possible research directions include developing new automated program verification techniques specifically for such programs, as well as specification inference, fault localisation or optimisation approaches that would make such verifiers practical usable for real-world code. The role also includes research administration, participation in project meetings, and may include up to 20% teaching within the Department’s course offerings (depending on the candidate's interest and course availability). We encourage all interested applicants to apply, even if their experience does not perfectly match the project's subject. We review all applications carefully and seek candidates who can contribute to the project's goals. Requirements PhD degree in computer science in a field relevant to the position such programming languages, program verification, or software engineering, or a foreign degree equivalent to a Swedish PhD degree in the subject. The degree needs to be obtained by the time of the decision of employment. Priority will be given to applicants who have completed their degree no more than three years before the application deadline. Due to special circumstances, the degree may have been obtained earlier. The three-year period can be extended due to circumstances such as sick leave, parental leave, duties in labour unions, etc. Fluency in both written and spoken English, and good programming skills are also a requirement. Additional qualifications We are searching for postdoc candidates who are responsible, self-motivated, and have demonstrated independence in research, and at the same time work well in a research group. Emphasis will also be placed on the ability to publish scientific work in high-quality venues and to give presentations at conferences and scientific meetings. Application procedure The application must include: a cover letter that briefly describes your motivation for applying for this position and this project and states the earliest possible date of employment (max 1 page); a curriculum vitae (CV); a research statement describing your previous research experience and current research interests (max two pages); a copy of relevant diplomas and grades (translated into Swedish or English, e.g. as provided by your university); a list of publications (may be included in CV); contact information for at least two references (do not include reference letters). About the employment The employment is a temporary position of two years according to central collective agreement. Full time position. Starting date 1 February 2027 or as agreed. Placement: Uppsala For further information about the position, please contact: Associate Professor Eva Darulova, e-mail: eva.darulova@it.uu.se. Please submit your application by 13 November 2026, UFV-PA 2026/2902. Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Department of Information Technology Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Temporary position Pay: Individual salary Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/2902 Last application date: 13 November 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=972009": {
      "title": "PhD student in hydrology",
      "description": "PhD student in hydrology - wildfires effect on Arctic water cycle - Uppsala University Use of cookies Uppsala University uses cookies to make your website experience better. Read more about cookies Accept all cookies Accept only necessary cookies Customize settings Skip to main content uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies PhD student in hydrology - wildfires effect on Arctic water cycle Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation PhD student in hydrology - wildfires effect on Arctic water cycle 2026-09-28 PhD student in hydrology with a focus on wildfires effect on Arctic water cycle Are you interested in working on cutting-edge research in hydrology, with the support of competent and friendly colleagues in an international environment? Are you looking for an employer that invests in sustainable employeeship and offers safe, favourable working conditions? We welcome you to apply for a PhD position at Uppsala University. The Department of Earth Sciences is Sweden´s most comprehensive academic environment for research and education in geoscience. It offers a broad range of expertise that can contribute to solving important societal issues. Earth is a dynamic and constantly changing planet. To understand how this planet works, our researchers seek answers in the field, through laboratory experiments and advanced models. Our research and education cover a wide range of disciplines, including rocks and minerals, weather and climate, the evolution of life, natural disasters, wind power and energy, environmental and water engineering, and sustainable development. Our research combines natural sciences and technology with social sciences and is often interdisciplinary. More than 300 people from over 30 countries work at the department, both in Uppsala and at Campus Gotland. Our six research divisions: • Geophysics • Air, Water and Landscape Science • Mineralogy, Petrology and Tectonics • Natural Resources and Sustainable Development • Palaeobiology • Wind Energy For more information see: www.uu.se/earthsciences The successful candidate will be enrolled in the Air, Water and Landscape Science programme (LUVAL). The position includes close collaboration with researchers at Uppsala University, SMHI and SLU, offering opportunities for interdisciplinary research, international networking, and engagement with societally relevant climate and environmental challenges. Project description The Arctic is rapidly warming, leading to changes in freshwater systems through melting glaciers, thawing permafrost, and shifting hydrological regimes. Understanding how these changes affect runoff generation, evapotranspiration, river discharge, and freshwater availability is a key challenge for Arctic hydrology. At the same time, wildfires activity is increasing across large parts of the Arctic, creating an additional disturbance that can alter vegetation, soils, permafrost conditions, and water flow paths. This PhD project will investigate how climate change and increasing wildfire activity are reshaping the Arctic water cycle. By combining Earth Observation (EO) satellite data with large-scale hydrological modelling, the doctoral student will study the impact of various wildfire-related landscape changes on hydrological processes in Arctic drainage basins. The project will generate new knowledge regarding the drivers and controls of hydrological changes in the Arctic and contribute to an improved understanding and better predictive models for future freshwater resources in northern regions. Duties The doctoral work consists of investigating how climate change and increasing wildfire activity affect hydrological processes across the Arctic. Duties include analysis of Earth Observation and hydrological data, hydrological modelling, and statistical analyses, as well as writing scientific articles. The PhD student will work with hydrologists from Uppsala University, SMHI and SLU, and is expected to contribute to the overall progress of the project. The doctoral education comprises four years of full-time studies, including courses and independent research. The applicant will also have the opportunity to participate in teaching, supervision, and other departmental duties, which may extend the employment by up to a maximum of 20%. Requirements To meet the entry requirements for doctoral studies, you must hold a Master’s (second-cycle) degree in Hydrology, Physical Geography, Geosciences, Environmental Sciences, Environmental engineering or another relevant subject, have completed at least 240 credits in higher education, with at least 60 credits at Master’s level including an independent project worth at least 15 credits, or have acquired substantially equivalent knowledge in some other way. Applicants must fulfill the above requirements before the admission can be started. You must also have good oral and written proficiency in English, strong quantitative and analytical skills, and experience in processing and analysing environmental or geospatial data. The position requires basic programming skills for scientific data analysis, the ability to work both independently and as part of a team, and a strong interest in hydrology and environmental change. Great emphasis will be placed on personal qualities such as analytical ability, initiative, creativity, flexibility and problem-solving skills. Additional qualifications Experience with hydrological modelling, remote sensing, GIS, and programming (e.g., Python or R) is considered an advantage. Knowledge of Arctic environments, cold-region hydrology, or wildfire impacts on ecosystems and water resources is meritorious. Rules governing PhD students are set out in the Higher Education Ordinance chapter 5, §§ 1-7 and in Uppsala University´s rules and guidelines . The application: In this recruitment we have replaced the cover letter with questions that you are asked to answer when making your application. The answers will be used as a part of the selection process. A Curriculum Vitae. A verified list of course grades, and a short description of your education. A copy of your master degree certificate. Your degree project/thesis report (finished or in draft form). The names and full contact information of two references (including e-mail address and phone no.) the application should be written in English About the employment The employment is a temporary position according to the Higher Education Ordinance chapter 5 § 7 . Scope of employment 100 %. Starting date 2027-01-15 or as agreed. Placement: Uppsala For further information about the position, please contact: Johanna Mård ( johanna.maard@geo.uu.se ) . Please submit your application by 30 of October, UFV-PA 2026/2820 Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Department of Earth Sciences Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Temporary position Pay: fast lön Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/2820 Last application date: 30 October 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=973333": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher in Sleep and Circadian Rhythms",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Researcher in Sleep and Circadian Rhythms - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Postdoctoral Researcher in Sleep and Circadian Rhythms 2026-09-28 Postdoctoral Researcher in Sleep and Circadian Rhythms Interventional and Translational Studies Integrating Physiology and Systems Biology The Department of Medical Cell Biology at Uppsala University is a strong and international research environment. The department has more than 110 employees, of which about 25 are doctoral students, 10 postdoctoral fellows, and 40 researchers, teachers and professors. Do you want to advance the understanding of how sleep and circadian rhythms shape human health? Are you passionate about integrating cutting-edge omics technologies with controlled human experiments and translational approaches? Join a leading research group at Uppsala University. About the position Sleep and circadian rhythms are fundamental regulators of cardiometabolic health, yet the molecular mechanisms linking them to disease remain incompletely understood. The Department of Medical Cell Biology at Uppsala University invites applications for a fully funded postdoctoral position (two years, with the possibility of a third year) focused on sleep and circadian biology (chronomedicine), cardiometabolic regulation, systems biology, and molecular mechanisms. The position offers substantial scope for scientific independence while being embedded in a supportive, interdisciplinary research environment with experienced principal investigators. We particularly welcome applicants who can bring expertise from computational biology, multi-omics, translational medicine, neuroscience, or related areas to questions in sleep and circadian physiology. Research enviroment The postdoctoral fellow will join a collaborative, internationally oriented research group with close links to Uppsala University Hospital, enabling bench-to-bedside research. Key resources include: Dedicated sleep laboratories for controlled sleep and circadian interventions Core facilities for sequencing, proteomics, metabolomics, and bioinformatics Access to unique clinical and population-based cohorts for translational validation Close collaborations with groups in diabetes, nutrition, molecular diagnostics, and omics bioinformatics Opportunities to integrate human experimental data with complementary clinical, computational, cellular, and preclinical approaches Your mission The overall aim is to advance mechanistic understanding of how sleep and circadian rhythms influence cardiometabolic health through molecular and genomic pathways, and their integration with physiological regulation. Key responsibilities include: Designing, coordinating, and contributing to interventional human clinical trials in sleep and circadian medicine, including high-resolution (e.g. 24-hour) and nighttime sampling Leading integrative multi-omics analyses (transcriptomics, metabolomics, proteomics, microbiome). Developing bioinformatic and statistical approaches for high-dimensional human data Integrating molecular findings with physiological, behavioral, clinical, and lifestyle data Contributing to manuscript preparation, grant applications, and development of new research directions Collaborating across disciplines to develop follow-up studies, including preclinical models, cellular systems, and cohort-based analyses Qualifications Required PhD in sleep research, circadian biology, bioinformatics, systems biology, neuroscience, molecular or translational medicine, or a related field (or equivalent foreign degree). The degree must be completed by the time of the employment decision and normally awarded no more than three years before the application deadline. Exceptions may be considered for documented special circumstances such as parental leave or sick leave. Documented experience, evidenced by peer-reviewed publications, in: (a) sleep and/or circadian rhythm research, or (b) bioinformatics and multi-omics integration (e.g. bulk or single-cell transcriptomics, spatial omics, proteomics, metabolomics, microbiome/metagenomics) Proficiency in analysis and visualization of complex biological data using R, Python, or similar Experience working with human data, preferably relating metabolic or cardiometabolic physiology and disease, such as obesity or type 2 diabetes, or other conditions with relevant metabolic components Strong interest in applying interdisciplinary expertise to sleep, circadian, and human physiological research Strong communication skills in written and spoken English Meritorious Familiarity with biological knowledge resources and reference atlases (e.g. Reactome, Gene Ontology, GTEx, Human Cell Atlas) Experience with multi-omics integration pipelines, quality control, and dimensionality reduction (e.g. PCA, t-SNE, PLS-DA) Data visualization tools (e.g. ggplot2, Illustrator) Experience in machine/deep learning, neural nets, generative AI models. Wet-lab or preclinical experience (e.g. ELISA, qPCR, Western blot, animal work), including experience with cell culture, stem-cell-derived models, organoids, imaging, or related experimental systems Experience with clinical trials, clinical cohorts, registry data, real-world data, or translational biomarker studies Participation in large research collaborations and project coordination What we offer A creative, international research environment at one of Scandinavia’s leading universities State-of-the-art infrastructure and dedicated sleep laboratories Competitive salary and benefits through Swedish collective agreements Opportunities for career development, independent research grants, national and international collaboration and conference participation Opportunities to develop expertise across human experimental physiology, sleep and circadian medicine, and integrative molecular approaches Read more about working at Uppsala University: https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ Application The application should be written in English or Swedish and include: Curriculum vitae (CV) A list of scientific publications A personal letter (max. 1 page) describing your background, research interests, motivation, and suitability for the position Contact details for 2-3 referees (name, e-mail, telephone) Copies of relevant diplomas and transcripts (as attachments) Applications are assessed on the basis of eligibility, documented experience, and individual suitability. About the employment The employment is a temporary position of 2 years according to central collective agreement. Full time position. Starting date as agreed. Placement: Uppsala For further information about the position, please contact: Jonathan Cedernaes, jonathan.cedernaes@mcb.uu.se Please submit your application by 19 October 2026 , UFV-PA 2026 /2879. Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Disciplinary Domain of Medicine and Pharmacy, Faculty of Medicine, Department of Medical Cell Biology Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Temporary position Pay: Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/2879 Last application date: 19 October 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=971754": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral position in Pharmacometrics with a focus on Regulatory Science",
      "description": "Postdoctoral position in Pharmacometrics with a focus on Regulatory Science - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Postdoctoral position in Pharmacometrics with a focus on Regulatory Science 2026-09-25 The Department of Pharmacy at Uppsala University has an interdisciplinary environment at the center of the pharmaceutical arena. With frontline research, first-rate education and extensive collaborations we constitute a driving force in the development of our academic field. In this inspiring environment our rich diversity of research groups, several of international prominence, develop and conduct work of great scientific importance. Among our core competencies are computational modelling and simulations, PKPD, in vitro ADME models, advanced in vivo methods, biological medicines, as well as patient and societal aspects, from optimising the use of drugs in individuals to societal pharmaceutical policies. Together, we form a unique cluster of academic competencies within pharmaceutical science, playing a key role in shaping the future of pharmacy in both Sweden and globally. Our scientific focus areas include: Pharmacokinetics & Pharmacodynamics • Pharmacometrics • Clinical Pharmacy • Advanced Drug Delivery • Molecular Pharmaceutics • Biological Drugs • Pharmacoepidemiology • Social Pharmacy More information www.farmaci.uu.se Duties/Project: Pharmacometric models describe the time course of disease and the effects of drugs on these time courses. The research group in Pharmacometrics is involved in methodological research concerning principles and approaches for the development and use of these types of models, as well as applied development and use of models in specific therapeutic areas to enhance the understanding of diseases and the effects of treatment, in order to streamline the development of new drugs and improve therapy with existing medicines. Much of our research is done in international collaboration with universities, industry and regulatory agencies in Europe, USA, Africa, Asia and Australia. The research team is international, with more than 12 nations and many areas of expertise (pharmaceutical sciences, engineering sciences, medicine, statistics and mathematics) represented. For more information about our research: Pharmacometrics We are now recruiting one postdoctoral fellow with a focus on regulatory science. The position is funded through an externally financed research project carried out in close collaboration with a drug regulatory agency. The project develops and evaluates model-based approaches for the design and analysis of clinical studies that support regulatory decision making, with the aim of making such studies more informative, efficient and robust. The work includes methodological development in pharmacometrics and biostatistics, extensive simulation studies to evaluate the statistical properties of the developed methods, analysis of clinical data, and implementation of the methods in open-source software in R. You will write scientific articles and technical reports, present results at international conferences, and take part in the ongoing dialogue with our partners in regulatory agencies and academia. Some supervision of students may also be included in the position. Qualifications: To qualify for an employment as a postdoctor you must have a PhD degree, or a foreign degree equivalent to a PhD degree, in pharmacometrics, pharmacokinetics/pharmacodynamics, statistics, biostatistics or a related field. The degree needs to be obtained by the time of the decision of employment. Priority will be given to applicants who have completed their degree no more than three years before the deadline for applications. Due to special circumstances, the degree may have been obtained earlier. The three-year period can be extended due to circumstances such as sick leave, parental leave, duties in labour unions, etc. We place great emphasis on personal suitability and motivation to improve methods within pharmacometrics and regulatory science. The applicant must be able to express themselves well, both orally and in writing, in English. Special merits: Experience of nonlinear mixed effects modelling (for example NONMEM, nlmixr2 or Monolix). Experience of clinical trial simulation and study design. Knowledge of statistical methodology for hypothesis testing and estimation of uncertainty. Good programming skills in R, preferably including development of software or R packages. Experience of regulatory questions or of collaboration with drug regulatory agencies. Interest in, and skill in, scientific writing is highly desirable, as is experience of collaborating in international networks. Application: The application should include: a motivation letter with a brief description of the candidate and research interests, as well as experiences in relation to the requirements and qualifications listed above, and the topics pharmacometrics, pharmacokinetics, pharmacodynamics, biostatistics and regulatory science the candidate's CV copies of diplomas and certificates recommendation letters, as well as other relevant documents that the applicant wishes to refer to, such as proficiency in English About the employment The employment is a temporary position of 2 years according to central collective agreement. Full time position. Starting date 2027-01-04 or as agreed. Placement: Uppsala For further information about the position, please contact: Professor Andrew Hooker, andrew.hooker@uu.se, and Professor Mats Karlsson, mats.karlsson@uu.se In this recruitment we have replaced the cover letter with questions that you are asked to answer when making your application. The answers will be used as a part of the selection process. Please submit your application by 23 October 2026 , UFV-PA 2026 /2809. Are you considering moving to Sweden to work at Uppsala University? Find out more about what it´s like to work and live in Sweden. Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Department of Pharmacy Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Temporary position Pay: Individuell lönesättning Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/2809 Last application date: 23 October 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
