    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=971937": {
      "title": "PhD student in laser spectroscopy",
      "description": "PhD student in laser spectroscopy - Uppsala University Use of cookies Uppsala University uses cookies to make your website experience better. Read more about cookies Accept all cookies Accept only necessary cookies Customize settings Skip to main content uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies PhD student in laser spectroscopy Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation PhD student in laser spectroscopy 2026-09-24 Are you interested in working with femtosecond lasers and their application to liquid-phase chemical reactions, with the support of competent and friendly colleagues in an international environment? Are you looking for an employer that invests in sustainable employeeship and offers safe, favourable working conditions? We welcome you to apply for a doctoral position at Uppsala University. The research conducted at the Department of Physics and Astronomy encompasses a wide range of physics topics, distributed over nine divisions. The department is located in the Ångström laboratory and employs nearly 400 people, 100 of whom are doctoral students. It offers a broad physics curriculum to undergraduate and graduate students, participation in nationally and internationally leading projects for researchers, and opportunities for partnership with industry and various outreach activities. Read more on www.uu.se/physics. The research will be conducted in the research program for Chemical and Bio-Molecular Physics at the Department of Physics and Astronomy at Uppsala University, which focuses on understanding the fundamental properties and ultrafast processes of matter at the atomic length and time scales of Ångströms and femtoseconds. The program has a leading position in the use of X-rays for probing atoms, molecules and chemical and biomolecular systems. We develop and apply novel X-ray methods and instrumentation and aim at revealing how the properties of a system result from its electronic structure and dynamics with applications in environmental, biophysical and chemical systems. Duties The PhD student will perform femtosecond laser spectroscopy experiments in the HELIOS laser laboratory operated by the division of X-ray Photon Science at Uppsala University. The goal is to study the charge dynamics during liquid-phase chemical reactions relevant to fields like light-harvesting and bond activation. The PhD student will contribute to the development of novel femtosecond THz and optical spectroscopy infrastructure and will design, execute, and analyze experiments aimed at understanding how molecular charge distributions drive chemical reactivity in catalysis. Additional responsibilities of the PhD student include the writing of scientific manuscripts, presentation of research findings at internal meetings and international conferences, as well as the active participation in collaborations with other experimental and theoretical groups. Requirements To meet the entry requirements for doctoral studies, you must hold a Master’s (second-cycle) degree in physics, chemistry (or related subject), or have completed at least 240 credits in higher education, with at least 60 credits at Master’s level including an independent project worth at least 15 credits, or have acquired substantially equivalent knowledge in some other way. The position also requires very good oral and written proficiency in English. Additional qualifications Very good knowledge of molecular physics and spectroscopy are considered an asset, as well as previous hands-on experience with laser spectroscopy and instrumentation. Experience with quantum chemical simulations is an advantage, but not necessarily required. Rules governing PhD students are set out in the Higher Education Ordinance chapter 5, §§ 1-7 and in Uppsala University's rules and guidelines . About the employment The employment is a temporary position according to the Higher Education Ordinance chapter 5 § 7. Scope of employment 100 %. Starting date 01-02-2027 or as agreed. Placement: Uppsala Information about doctoral education, eligibility requirements and admission rules can be found on the web site of the Faculty of Science and Technology . For further information about the position, please contact: Dr. Raphael Jay, +46 76-022 67 04, raphael.jay@physics.uu.se. In this recruitment we have replaced the cover letter with questions that you are asked to answer when making your application. The answers will be used as a part of the selection process. Please submit your application by 20 November 2026, UFV-PA 2026/2816. Are you considering moving to Sweden to work at Uppsala University? Find out more about what it´s like to work and live in Sweden . Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Department of Physics and Astronomy Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Temporary position Pay: Fixed salary Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/2816 Last application date: 20 November 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=972555": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral position in computational chemistry",
      "description": "Postdoctoral position in computational chemistry - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Postdoctoral position in computational chemistry 2026-09-24 Are you interested in working with computational chemistry, with the support of competent and friendly colleagues in an international environment? Are you looking for an employer that invests in sustainable employeeship and offers safe, favourable working conditions? We welcome you to apply for a postdoctoral position at Uppsala University. The research program for computational biology and bioinformatics at the department for cell and molecular biology hosts a large variety of research topics, from sequence-based bioinformatics, drug design and enzymology to development of methods in computational chemistry. The group led by Prof. David van der Spoel performs research on force fields for molecular simulation. They have developed a machine learning software, the Alexandria Chemistry Toolkit, that based on quantum-chemistry calculations derives complete force fields. This tool gives us unique possibilities to put a new subtopic of computational chemistry, force field science, on the map. Read more at https://www.uu.se/en/department/cell-and-molecular-biology/research/computational-biology-and-bioinformatics/van-der-spoel-lab . This Postdoc position is part of the eSSENCE graduate school in data-intensive science. The school addresses the challenge of data-intensive science both from the foundational methodological perspective and from the perspective of data-driven science applications. It is an arena where experts in computational science, data science and data engineering (systems and methodology) work closely together with researchers in (data-driven) sciences, industry and society to accelerate data-intensive scientific discovery. eSSENCE is a strategic collaborative research programme in e-science between three Swedish universities with a strong tradition of excellent e-science research: Uppsala University, Lund University and Umeå University. https://www.essenceofescience.se/ Duties You will work in a new collaboration with Prof. Daniel Brandell, Chemistry-Ångström, with the topic of “Machine learning to design electrolytes for sodium batteries”. To reduce environmental pressure related to battery production, we will work on batteries using sodium rather than lithium as charge carriers. You will perform quantum chemistry calculations, train new force field models, perform molecular dynamics simulations, and validate the force fields with both quantum chemistry and experimental data that will be produced by the lab of Prof. Brandell. The materials you design may be synthesized by our collaborators for direct experimental feedback. Requirements PhD degree in chemistry or a degree equivalent to a PhD degree in chemistry. The degree needs to be obtained by the time of the decision of employment. Priority will be given to applicants who have completed their degree no more than three years before the deadline for applications.  Due to special circumstances, the degree may have been obtained earlier. The three-year period can be extended due to circumstances such as sick leave, parental leave, duties in labour unions, etc. Other qualification requirements: good working knowledge of organic and inorganic chemistry, documented experience of computational chemistry, documented experience of Python programming, social competence, since you will be working in a collaboration project, fluency in the English language. Additional qualifications Experience with high-performance computing, experience of programming in C++, experience of software development in a team, experience of battery research, as well as experience of working in a Linux environment. About the employment The employment is a temporary position of two years according to central collective agreement. Full time position. Starting date 2017-01-01 or as agreed. Placement: Uppsala. For further information about the position, please contact: David van der Spoel, +46184714205, david.vanderspoel@icm.uu.se In this recruitment we have replaced the cover letter with questions that you are asked to answer when making your application. The answers will be used as a part of the selection process. Please submit your application by October 30th 2026, UFV-PA 2026/2843. Are you considering moving to Sweden to work at Uppsala University? Find out more about what it´s like to work and live in Sweden. Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Department of Cell and Molecular Biology Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Temporary position Pay: Individuell lönesättning Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/2843 Last application date: 30 October 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=972884": {
      "title": "About the position",
      "description": "Postdoctoral position in advanced structural analysis and electrochemical applications of carbon materials  - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Postdoctoral position in advanced structural analysis and electrochemical applications of carbon materials 2026-09-24 The Department of Chemistry - Ångström conducts research and education in the chemistry field. The department has more than 270 employees and has a turnover of 300 million SEK. At the department's six programs, we conduct very successful research of a high international standard. We have a large number of externally funded research projects, often with international cooperation and we see continued good growth in our subject area. The department has education assignments in engineering programs and master's programs. More information is available on our website . (https://kemi.uu.se/angstrom/?languageId=1). About the position Applications are invited from highly competent and motivated candidates for a postdoctoral research position to develop and characterize carbon materials, such as natural graphite, porous carbon and hard carbon, intended for energy storage applications. The successful candidate will join a collaborative project involving Uppsala University (UU), industrial partners and research institutes, contributing to a highly interdisciplinary effort to establish comprehensive structure–electrochemistry relationships in disordered carbon and natural graphite used in electrochemical applications. Both experimental and theoretical skills are considered essential. The researcher will primarily design and execute total X-ray and neutron scattering experiments, using pair distribution function (PDF) analysis to elucidate the short- and medium-range atomic order in disordered materials, and will employ small-angle X-ray and neutron scattering to probe the pore microstructure and morphological characteristics of the materials. Researchers with prior experience using molecular dynamics simulations and machine learning methods to study the structure and electrochemistry of disordered materials are also encouraged to apply. The project primarily aims to understand the complex structure of disordered carbon based on experimental data, employ novel structural and electrochemical methods, identify the properties that influence electrochemical behaviour, and establish the correlation between structure and electrochemical characteristics of different types of carbon materials. The researcher should, thus, be well-versed in both theoretical and experimental electrochemistry and have expertise in a wide range of materials characterization techniques, including total X-ray and neutron scattering and pair distribution function (PDF) analysis, small-angle X-ray scattering (SAXS), and advanced data analysis. Most of the research will be carried out in the battery research laboratories, which are equipped with state-of-the-art facilities for materials synthesis, characterization (XPS, Raman spectroscopy, X-ray diffraction, thermal analysis, etc.), electrode fabrication, cell assembly and electrochemical testing. A full suite of electron microscopy (SEM and TEM) and surface analysis tools is also available in the cleanroom facility at the Ångström Laboratory. In addition to the resources at UU, the researcher will have access to national and international research infrastructure such as MAX IV. Work duties The main duties of the post-doctoral employee are to conduct research. Teaching and other departmental responsibilities may also be included, up to no more than 20% of working hours. The successful candidate will work in a large research group consisting of students and researchers. The candidate is expected to conduct high-quality research within the project, ultimately resulting in patents and publications in peer-reviewed journals or conference proceedings work in close collaboration with the principal investigator and project partners maintain up-to-date knowledge, and gather data relevant to the project take initiative in identifying research gaps and future research directions related to the project participate in the supervision and teaching of undergraduate and doctoral students contribute to writing research proposals to attract external funding prepare periodic reports to be submitted to the granting agency present and disseminate research results at international conferences, group seminars, and regular project meetings design proper experimental procedures taking laboratory safety into account ensure compliance with laboratory, environmental and health safety regulations maintain a strong commitment to the implementation of research ethics Requirements To be considered for this position, applicants must have a PhD degree in chemistry, materials science or a related subject when submitting the application. Priority will be given to applicants who have obtained their PhD within the last three years. Circumstances such as parental leave or career breaks due to illness or trade union duties will not, however, be included in the time calculation. Excellent command of verbal and written English is required. The candidate must have a strong background in both experimental and theoretical electrochemistry and documented experience in the structure analysis of disordered materials such as hard carbon and battery testing. We attach great importance to personal qualities such as creative mentality, team spirit and strong motivation to work independently as well as in collaboration with project partners. In addition, the research post requires organized documentation of laboratory procedures and curating data suitable for publication and patenting. Essential qualifications Strong expertise in two or more of the following research areas is necessary: synthesis, functionalization and characterization of carbon materials used in batteries in-depth understanding of the different components of sodium-, or lithium-ion batteries or other similar devices understanding of theoretical electrochemistry and skills in electrochemical methods (voltammetry, galvanostatic techniques, electrochemical impedance analysis and so on) Raman spectroscopy (highly desired skill, especially in the characterization of carbon-based materials) small-angle X-ray/neutron scattering (SAXS/SANS), total X-ray scattering and pair distribution function (PDF) analysis on carbon materials electron microscopy (SEM and/or TEM) data analysis, machine learning and molecular dynamics simulations of the structure and electrochemistry of disordered materials, preferably carbon We particularly encourage applications from candidates who can bring novel technical skills (synchrotron or other large-scale facilities) that can be applied in the study of the structure and electrochemistry of disordered materials (such as hard carbons). Desirable/Additional qualifications Experience in both industrial and academic research in battery manufacturing is desirable. Prior experience in laboratory and project management is also advantageous. Programming skills or acquaintance with applying Python packages, statistical data analysis packages, machine learning etc are a strong advantage. At a postdoctoral research position, the candidate is primarily tasked with research but teaching duties may be included in the job description at the discretion of the department, but not more than 20 % of working hours. Thus, previous teaching experience at the undergraduate or graduate level is also highly valued. About the employment The employment is a temporary position for 2 years according to the central collective agreement. Scope of employment 100 % (full-time, 40 hours per week) Starting date 1 January 2027 or as agreed. Placement: Uppsala For further information about the position, please contact: Dr. Habtom D. Asfaw, habtom.desta.asfaw@kemi.uu.se Application procedure Applications must be submitted online using the link below. Assessment of applications will be based on academic background, research expertise, relevant publications, ability to conduct reliable and independent research, and collaborative skills. Your application must include a cover letter (maximum 1 page) with a short description of yourself, the reasons why you are interested in the position, and your previous research experience. a short CV (maximum 2 pages). Please provide in your CV a link to download a copy of your PhD thesis if it is available online. a list of papers and conference contributions. At least one first-author publication is required to demonstrate the writing skills and scientific rigour of the candidate. Greater emphasis is laid on the quality rather than the number of publications. the names and contact details of 2-3 persons who are available to act as references for you upon request. authorized copies of your degrees, transcripts and other relevant documents (merits) can be included as well. All original documents to be submitted must be issued in English or Swedish, or else notarized translations must be provided. Please do not attach any manuscripts, papers, or irrelevant certificates as these will not be considered as part of your application. Please submit your application by 26 October 2026, UFV-PA 2026/2862. Interviews of shortlisted candidates will be scheduled shortly after, and you must be available to meet via Zoom. Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Disciplinary Domain of Science and Technology, Faculty of Chemistry, Department of Chemistry - Ångström Laboratory Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Temporary position Pay: Individuell lönesättning Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/2862 Last application date: 26 October 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=967825": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Mathematics specialising in Analysis and Probability",
      "description": "Assistant Professor in Mathematics specialising in Analysis and Probability - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Assistant Professor in Mathematics specialising in Analysis and Probability 2026-09-23 Do you want to be part of an outstanding research environment within mathematics and move your research forward at the largest faculty of science and technology in Sweden? We are now looking for an associate senior lecturer who wants to be part of developing our research and education in analysis and probability. At our workplace on Campus Ångström, the Department of mathematics, with its 120 employees, does research and education. The research is subdivided into three programs: algebra and geometry, analysis and probability, and applied mathematics and statistics. We educate at the research-, the advanced, and the basic level. The department holds courses in mathematics and mathematical statistics within several different educational programs: a number of different civil engineering programs, teacher’s programs, various bachelor programs at the faculty of science and technology as well as our own bachelor and master programs in mathematics. You can read more about the research and education in the mathematics department at www.math.uu.se. Subject area The subject area of the position is analysis and probability. Of particular interest is connections between complex analysis, probability theory, and mathematical physics. Duties You will work with: research. Actively applying for and securing external grants. teaching. Teaching includes responsibility for courses, course administration and supervision of doctoral students. administration. Participate in the general academic duties of Department of mathematics. This includes serving on committees, taking on responsibilities beyond your own research and teaching assignments, contributing to the evaluation and development of teaching and research activities, working collaboratively with colleagues, and providing support and constructive feedback to colleagues. keeping up to date in your subject area and following developments in society that are relevant to your work at Uppsala University. In choosing between eligible candidates, emphasis will primarily be given to both research and teaching expertise, which will be accorded equal weight. Qualifications required You must have: a PhD in mathematics. Preference will be given to applicants who have completed their PhD or attained equivalent expertise no more than seven years before the deadline for applications. research expertise in analysis and probability, in particular connections between complex analysis, probability theory, and mathematical physics. teaching expertise, according particular weight to teaching in mathematics. The ability to integrate research in the relevant subject area, subject didactic, and higher education into teaching is also required. completed at least five weeks of teacher training for higher education of relevance to the organisation and its activities or be considered to have acquired the equivalent knowledge. The required training for teachers in higher education may be completed during the first two years of employment if there are special circumstances. a documented ability to teach in Swedish and English unless there are special reasons. ability to work with other people and otherwise meet the demands of suitability required to perform the duties well. a documented ability to obtain external grants. teaching expertise and research expertise that are relevant to the subject area and the duties that the position involves. For more information on assessment and assessment criteria, see the Appointment Regulations for Uppsala University and the Faculty of Science and Technology’s Guidelines for the Appointement and Promotion of Teachers . All qualifications must be documented in a manner that makes it possible to assess both their quality and their scope. When the University appoints new academic staff, candidates will be selected based on a qualitative overall assessment of their competence and expertise, taking into account their potential to perform and develop the duties of the position and to contribute to the positive development of the department. Application Parental leave, part-time work due to childcare, trade union responsibilities, military service or similar activities are treated as work experience and should be listed in the CV. Instructions for applications for employment Period of employment The position of Assistant Professor is fixed-term for up to six years and is intended to provide qualifications for a permanent teaching position with higher eligibility requirements. During the appointment, there is the possibility to apply for promotion to Associate Professor. If the requirements are met and suitability is confirmed, the appointee may be promoted to a permanent position as Associate Professor. About the position This is a temporary full-time position six years. The position is full-time (100%). Starting date May 1 or as agreed. Place of work: Uppsala Further information about the position is available from: Head of department, professor Tobias Ekholm, tobias.ekholm@math.uu.se We look forward to receiving your application by 6 November 2026, UFV-PA 2026-2673. In the event of any disagreement between the English and the Swedish versions of this announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. We offer you Sweden offers good working conditions, including comprehensive social benefits such as generous family-focused policies that make healthcare, childcare, and children’s education available and highly affordable. At Uppsala University, we offer the opportunity for new international staff to learn Swedish through our language courses. If you have family, they will get new contacts and support through the Uppsala International Citizen hub . If you are an international candidate, you will find a lot of information about working and living in Sweden at http://www.uu.se/joinus . Uppsala University’s tenure track system grants assistant professors the possibility to be assessed for promotion to the position as associate professor. The university provides support in various areas, such as scientific and educational development, leadership development as well as patent and innovation support. Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Disciplinary Domain of Science and Technology, Faculty of Mathematics and Computer Science, Department of Mathematics Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Temporary position Pay: Individually negotiated salary Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/2673 Last application date: 6 November 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=972267": {
      "title": "PhD student in Machine Learning with a focus on mathematical and statistical methods for uncertainty quantification",
      "description": "PhD student in Machine Learning with a focus on mathematical and statistical methods for uncertainty quantification - Uppsala University Use of cookies Uppsala University uses cookies to make your website experience better. Read more about cookies Accept all cookies Accept only necessary cookies Customize settings Skip to main content uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies PhD student in Machine Learning with a focus on mathematical and ... Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation PhD student in Machine Learning with a focus on mathematical and statistical methods for uncertainty quantification 2026-09-23 Are you interested in probability theory, statistics, and mathematical modelling? Would you like to develop new methods for uncertainty quantification and apply these methods to large-scale clinical cancer data? Are you looking for an employer that invests in sustainable employeeship and offers safe, favorable working conditions? We welcome you to apply for a PhD position at the Department of Information Technology, Uppsala University. The Department of Information Technology holds a leading position in both research and education at all levels. We are currently Uppsala University's third largest department, have around 350 employees, including 120 teachers and 120 PhD students. Approximately 5,000 undergraduate students take one or more courses at the department each year. You can find more information about us on the Department of Information Technology website . At the Division of Systems and Control , we develop both theory and concrete tools to design systems that learn, reason, and act in the real world based on a seamless combination of data, mathematical models, and algorithms. Our research integrates expertise from machine learning, optimization, control theory, and applied mathematics, spanning diverse application domains such as medicine, energy systems, biomedical systems, neuroscience, and safety and security. The Division of Systems and Control enjoys a wide network of strong international collaborators all around the world, for example at the University of Oxford, the University of Melbourne, and the University of California, Los Angeles. We strive for all PhD students to get a solid international experience during their PhD. About the DDLS Fellows program The PhD position is part of the national research programme DDLS. Data-driven life science (DDLS) uses data, computational methods and artificial intelligence to study biological systems and processes at all levels, from molecular structures and cellular processes to human health and global ecosystems. The SciLifeLab and Wallenberg National Program for Data-Driven Life Science (DDLS) aims to recruit and train the next generation of data-driven life scientists and to create globally leading computational and data science capabilities in Sweden. The program is funded with a total of 3.3 billion SEK over 12 years from the Knut and Alice Wallenberg (KAW) Foundation. In 2026 the DDLS Research School will be expanded with the recruitment of 25 academic and 7 industrial PhD students. During the course of the DDLS program more than 260 PhD students and 200 postdocs will be part of the Research School. The DDLS program has four strategic research areas: cell and molecular biology, evolution and biodiversity, precision medicine and diagnostics, epidemiology and biology of infection. For more information, please see: https://www.scilifelab.se/data-driven/ddls-research-school/ The future of life science is data-driven. Will you be part of that change? Then join us in this unique program! At Uppsala University, we are announcing the position as DDLS PhD student in data-driven precision medicine and diagnostics. Data-driven precision medicine and diagnostics covers data integration, analysis, visualization, and data interpretation for patient stratification, discovery of biomarkers for disease risks, diagnosis, drug response and monitoring of health. The precision medicine research is expected to make use of existing strong assets in Sweden and abroad, such as molecular data (e.g. omics), imaging, electronic health care records, longitudinal patient and population registries and biobanks. Project description Data-driven mathematical and statistical models are increasingly used in life science research and healthcare. Quantifying the uncertainty associated with these models is crucial for understanding their reliability and for making informed decisions based on their predictions. This project aims to develop new methods for uncertainty quantification in mathematical and statistical models. The methods will be applied to large-scale clinical cancer data. A central application will be quantifying uncertainty in information extracted from medical reports and propagating this uncertainty into downstream probabilistic time-to-event models. Duties The doctoral student will primarily devote their time to graduate education. Other departmental duties of at most 20%, including teaching and administration, may also be included in the employment. Requirements To meet the general entry requirements for doctoral studies, you must: hold a Master’s (second-cycle) degree in applied mathematics, applied statistics, engineering physics, physics, machine learning, or in a similar subject, or have completed at least 240 credits in higher education, with at least 60 credits at Master’s level including an independent project worth at least 15 credits, or have acquired substantially equivalent knowledge in some other way. The University may permit an exemption from the general entry requirements for an individual applicant, if there are special grounds (Chapter 7, § 39 of the Higher Education Ordinance). For special entry requirements, please see the subject’s general study plan . We are looking for candidates with: strong foundations in linear algebra, probability theory, and calculus solid skills in programming interest in mathematical and statistical method development, good communication skills and sufficient proficiency in oral and written English, creativity, thoroughness, and a structured approach to problem-solving Additional qualifications Experience with one or more of the following areas is meriting: Bayesian statistics, mathematical modelling, statistical machine learning. Rules governing PhD students are set out in the Higher Education Ordinance chapter 5, §§ 1-7 and in Uppsala University's rules and guidelines . Application The application must include: a one-page cover letter outlining how you meet the required criteria, your motivation for applying to this position, and your expected earliest starting date; a CV; degrees and transcript of records with grades (translated to English or Swedish); a Master’s thesis (or a draft thereof, and/or some other self-produced technical or scientific text), publications, and other relevant documents; references with contact information (names, emails and telephone number), and up to two reference letters. About the employment The employment is a temporary position according to the Higher Education Ordinance chapter 5 § 7. Scope of employment 100 %. Starting date 15 November 2026 or as otherwise agreed. Placement: Uppsala. For further information about the position, please contact: Assistant Professor Sara Hamis, e-mail: sara.hamis@it.uu.se. Please submit your application by 16 October 2026, UFV-PA 2026/2836. Are you considering moving to Sweden to work at Uppsala University? Find out more about what it´s like to work and live in Sweden . Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Department of Information Technology Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Temporary position Pay: Fixed salary Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/2836 Last application date: 16 October 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
