    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=978806": {
      "title": "Research Assistant in Work Environment, Parenthood and Academic Careers",
      "description": "Research Assistant in Work Environment, Parenthood and Academic Careers - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Research Assistant in Work Environment, Parenthood and Academic Careers 2026-10-15 Are you interested in issues related to workplace environment, gender equality, and career development in academia? Would you like to contribute to a research project aimed at improving the conditions for employees on parental leave and employees with young children? We welcome applications for a position as Research Assistant at the Department of Earth Sciences, Uppsala University. The Department of Earth Sciences is Sweden\"s most comprehensive academic environment for research and education in geoscience. It offers a broad range of expertise that can contribute to solving important societal issues. Earth is a dynamic and constantly changing planet. To understand how this planet works, our researchers seek answers in the field, through laboratory experiments and advanced models. Our research and education cover a wide range of disciplines, including rocks and minerals, weather and climate, the evolution of life, natural disasters, wind power and energy, environmental and water engineering, and sustainable development. Our research combines natural sciences and technology with social sciences and is often interdisciplinary. More than 300 people from over 30 countries work at the department, both in Uppsala and at Campus Gotland. Our six research divisions: • Geophysics • Air, Water and Landscape Science • Mineralogy, Petrology and Tectonics • Natural Resources and Sustainable Development • Palaeobiology • Wind Energy For more information see: www.uu.se/earthsciences This position is linked to a project that aims to map how employees on parental leave and employees with young children experience their work environment, support structures, and career opportunities at Uppsala University. The project will initially focus on the Department of Earth Sciences and the Disciplinary Domain of Science and Technology. Through surveys, interviews, and analysis of existing support systems, the project seeks to identify both challenges and examples of good practice in order to contribute to the development of evidence-based measures and a more inclusive working environment. Duties As a Research Assistant, you will work closely with the project leader and contribute to the implementation of the project. Duties include, but are not limited to: Conducting literature searches and reviewing relevant research. Assisting in the development and design of a survey. Administering and compiling survey data. Planning, conducting, and documenting interviews. Processing and analyzing qualitative and quantitative data. Mapping information and support resources provided by the University and its HR functions. Compiling results in reports and presentations. Providing practical support in the day-to-day work of the project. The duties may evolve depending on the needs of the project and the qualifications of the successful candidate. As a Research Assistant, you must be able to work to deadlines. The role involves independently handling multiple tasks and managing ongoing work assignments as they arise. Qualifications Higher education or equivalent qualifications deemed appropriate by the employer, together with relevant work experience. Experience of research work or research-related administration. Experience with survey studies, interviews, or qualitative data analysis. Knowledge of statistics and quantitative analysis. Experience in writing reports or scientific texts. Excellent communication skills and the ability to use language in a professional manner relevant to the position. Good proficiency in both Swedish and English, spoken and written, as well as excellent computer skills, particularly in Microsoft Office. We are looking for a person who is collaborative, service-oriented, and flexible. You are responsible, thorough, and systematic, with the ability to maintain an overview of several ongoing processes simultaneously. The ability to work independently and with good planning and organizational skills is essential. Great emphasis will be placed on personal suitability. Additional Qualifications Interest in workplace environment, equality, or organizational issues. Experience of working at Uppsala University or a similar higher education institution. About the Employment The position is fixed-term for five months. The scope of employment is 50%. Starting date: 1 December 2026, or as agreed. Place of work: Uppsala. Further information about the position can be obtained from: Steffi Burchardt Telephone: +46 72 200 33 20 Email: steffi.burchardt@geo.uu.se Welcome to submit your application no later than 29 October 2026, reference number UFV-PA 2026/3083. Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Department of Earth Sciences Scope: Part-time Working hours: 50% Type of employment: Temporary position Pay: Individuell lönesättning Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/3083 Last application date: 29 October 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=978899": {
      "title": "Cheftekniker",
