    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=978687": {
      "title": "20% Teaching Assistants",
      "description": "20% Teaching Assistants - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation 20% Teaching Assistants 2026-10-13 The Department of Information Technology holds a leading position in both research and education at all levels. We are currently Uppsala University's third largest department, have around 350 employees, including 120 teachers and120 PhD students. Approximately 5,000 undergraduate students take one or more courses at the department each year. You can find more information about us on the Department of Information Technology website. Are you interested in education and being part of an academic work environment? Do you want experience in working at a university? The Department of Information Technology is looking for 20% teaching assistants (TAs) for the spring 2027. 20% TAs are teaching assistants hired for a whole academic year. As a 20%-teaching assistant you are the department’s employee and part of the department's operations. You get an insight into the University and get to be a part of the daily work at one of the departments divisions. You will participate in the teaching and administration of selected programs and courses at the department and in the activities organized at your division. As a 20%-TA you have access to staff space and office space, and you also get to take part in the university's many employment benefits, such as healthcare benefits and paid vacation days. Duties Participation in teaching in courses at the Department of Information Technology. Participation in teaching means, for example, participation in labs and tutorials/lessons, grading of assignments, answering students' questions, supervision of student projects or course evaluations. Requirements Employment as a student assistant is regulated by the Higher Education Ordinance, Chapter 5. Only those who are admitted to education at the undergraduate or advanced level may be employed as student assistants (Higher Education Ordinance, Chapter 5 §10). The applicant must show good study results, especially in the area of the course the applicant will help with, as well as very good English communication skills, both spoken and written. Additional qualifications Previous experience from participating in teaching in courses at university level is particularly meritorious. Experience with relevant IT systems (Studium) is desirable as well as good knowledge of Uppsala University's organization. Good Swedish communication skills, both spoken and written (only for courses taught in Swedish). Application procedure The application should include a letter in which the applicant briefly describes his/her experience in teaching, language and knowledge (e.g., study certificate). Please also describe and justify why you are interested in the position. The application may also include information on the courses that the applicant prefers to teach. Please also attach your registration certificate. Interviews are scheduled for the 16th to the 18th of November 2026. About the employment The employment is a temporary position according to the Higher Education Ordinance chapter 5 § 12 until the 20th of June 2027. Scope of employment: 20 %. Starting date: 18th of January or as agreed. Placement: Uppsala. For further information about the position, please contact: Head of Recruitment Davide Vega D'Aurelio (ugarekrytering-it@uu.se) Please submit your application by Monday the 26th of October 2026, UFV-PA 2026/3079. Are you considering moving to Sweden to work at Uppsala University? Find out more about what it´s like to work and live in Sweden . Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Department of Information Technology Scope: Part-time Working hours: 20% Type of employment: Temporary position Pay: Individual salary Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representatives: ST/TCO ST/TCO tco@fackorg.uu.se Seko Universitetsklubben seko@uadm.uu.se Saco-rådet Saco-rådet saco@uadm.uu.se Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/3079 Last application date: 26 October 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
