    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=984023": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral position in structure-based drug design using machine learning",
      "description": "Postdoctoral position in structure-based drug design using machine learning - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Postdoctoral position in structure-based drug design using machine learning 2026-10-27 Are you interested in developing virtual screening techniques to discover novel drugs? We welcome you to apply for a postdoctoral position in the international and scientifically excellent research environment at the Department of Cell and Molecular Biology, Uppsala University. The Department of Cell and Molecular Biology ( https://icm.uu.se ) is organized into seven research programs focusing on Computational Biology and Bioinformatics, Microbiology and Immunology, Molecular Biology, Molecular Biophysics, Molecular Evolution, Molecular Systems Biology, and Structural Biology. The position is available in the research group led by Prof. Jens Carlsson, which is part of the Computational Biology and Bioinformatics program. The Carlsson group develops and applies molecular modeling techniques to study protein-ligand interactions, particularly how receptors and enzymes interact with drugs. G protein-coupled receptors (GPCRs) are a key research area for the Carlsson group because of their important roles in physiological processes. The Carlsson group uses structure-based models to understand the molecular mechanisms of GPCR signaling and to design ligands for these pharmaceutically important targets, often in close collaboration with experimental groups. The Carlsson group is an international research team and is also affiliated with the Science for Life Laboratory ( http://www.scilifelab.se/ ). Visit the group website for more information ( www.carlssonlab.org ). Duties The main goals of the project are to develop and apply structure-based virtual screening techniques to identify ligands for peptide-binding GPCRs in large chemical libraries. The project will use molecular docking and machine learning techniques to screen for ligands in combinatorial libraries of peptides and peptidomimetics, as well as in collections of naturally occurring peptides from microbes, plants, and animals. The project also involves collaborations with experimental research groups within the Biodiversity2Drugs consortium ( https://www.biodiversa.eu/2025/04/08/biodiversity2drugs /), which focus on identifying bioactive peptides that target GPCRs of therapeutic relevance. Requirements PhD degree in computational chemistry or a foreign degree equivalent to a PhD degree in computational chemistry. The degree needs to be obtained by the time of the decision of employment. Priority will be given to applicants who have completed their degree no more than three years before the deadline for applications. Due to special circumstances, the degree may have been obtained earlier. The three-year period can be extended due to circumstances such as sick leave, parental leave, duties in labour unions, etc. Strong expertise in computational chemistry, with demonstrated experience in cheminformatics and structure-based ligand design, is required. Proficiency in molecular docking or co-folding methods for predicting protein–ligand complexes and experience in working with chemical libraries are also required. Excellent written and spoken English is required as the work takes place in an international environment. We attach great importance to personal qualities, in particular good collaborative abilities, motivation, creativity and independence. Additional qualifications Experience in machine learning, scientific programming, and structure-based modeling of GPCRs and peptides is preferred but not required. About the employment The employment is a temporary position of two years according to central collective agreement. Full time position. Starting date 2027-01-01 or as agreed. Placement: Uppsala. For further information about the position, please contact: Jens Carlsson, jens.carlsson@icm.uu.se, Tel: +46 (0)72 227 7976. In this recruitment we have replaced the cover letter with questions that you are asked to answer when making your application. The answers will be used as a part of the selection process. Please submit your application by 23 November 2026, UFV-PA 2026/3253. Are you considering moving to Sweden to work at Uppsala University? Find out more about what it´s like to work and live in Sweden. Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Department of Cell and Molecular Biology Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Temporary position Pay: Individuell lönesättning Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/3253 Last application date: 23 November 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=984196": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral position in Computational Materials Chemistry",
      "description": "Postdoctoral position in Computational Materials Chemistry - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Postdoctoral position in Computational Materials Chemistry 2026-10-27 The Department of Chemistry - Ångström conducts research and education in the chemistry field. The department has more than 270 employees and has a turnover of 300 million SEK. At the department's six programs, we conduct very successful research of a high international standard. We have a large number of externally funded research projects, often with international cooperation and we see continued good growth in our subject area. The department has education assignments in engineering programs and master's programs. More information is available on our website . Duties The goal of the research project is to improve the understanding of mechanisms governing ion transport in ceramic-polymer composite electrolytes for solid-state batteries and provide guidelines for developing materials with improved ionic conductivity. The work focuses on method development and on developing and applying computationally efficient multiscale models, with particular emphasis on statistical thermodynamics and probability-based dynamical methods, such as molecular dynamics and kinetic Monte Carlo, to study transport within and between the different material phases. Atomistic simulations and experimental data will be used to develop and validate the models, with particular emphasis on the role of interphases in ion transport. The project is funded by the Swedish Energy Agency and will be conducted within the Structural Chemistry research programme at Uppsala University which encompasses both Computational Materials Chemistry and the Ångström Advanced Battery Centre (ÅABC). The postdoctoral researcher will be an active member of both research environments. The project is conducted in collaboration with LEPMI at Grenoble INP in France . The work also includes a research stay of approximately two months per year at Grenoble INP. Requirements For employment as postdoc, the applicant should have a PhD degree or an international equivalent within the field of Chemistry, Physics, Materials Science or other for the position relevant fields, within a maximum of three (3) years before the final application date. During certain circumstances, an earlier PhD can be acceptable. Certain circumstances include leave due to illness, maternity leave, in trade unions, etc. The assessment of applications is based primarily on the applicant's ability to conduct independent research based on scientific skill. Greater importance will be attached to the quality of individual scientific work, than to the number of publications. The applicant is expected to have a very good knowledge of written and spoken English. A solid background in computational chemistry methods spanning different length and time scales, including dynamical simulations, and a strong foundation in statistical thermodynamics are required. The applicant must have experience of and ability to collaborate with experimental researchers, the ability to build effective teams, and leadership abilities that support the supervision of PhD and master’s students. The ability to communicate science clearly, both orally and in writing, is also required. These abilities will carry substantial weight in the assessment. Additional qualifications Experience in method development and modelling of materials, transport mechanisms and interphases is advantageous, as are programming skills and experience with machine learning. About the employment The employment is a temporary position of 2 years according to central collective agreement. Full-time position. Starting date 2027-01-01 or as agreed. Placement: Uppsala For further information about the position, please contact: Amber Mace, email: amber.mace@kemi.uu.se In this recruitment we have replaced the cover letter with questions that you are asked to answer when making your application. The answers will be used as a part of the selection process. Please submit your application by 30th Novmeber 2026, UFV-PA 2026/3260. Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Disciplinary Domain of Science and Technology, Faculty of Chemistry, Department of Chemistry - Ångström Laboratory Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Temporary position Pay: Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/3260 Last application date: 30 November 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
