    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=981585": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral researcher in chemistry with specialization in organic chemistry",
      "description": "Postdoctoral researcher in chemistry with specialization in organic chemistry  - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Postdoctoral researcher in chemistry with specialization in organic chemistry 2026-10-23 Department of Chemistry for Life Sciences conducts research and education in analytical chemistry, biochemistry and organic chemistry. More than 100 people work at the department. New employees and students are recruited from all over the world and English is the main working language. The department is located at the Biomedical Centre in Uppsala, which facilitates collaborations with research groups in biology, pharmacy, medicine and SciLifeLab and gives access to advanced infrastructure for experimental and theoretical studies. You can find more information about us here . This project aims to develop NOESY-based ensemble analysis methods for medium-sized molecules, such as macrocycles and PROTACs. The postdoctoral researcher’s specific task involves NMR spectroscopic measurements and the interpretation of spectroscopic data. Duties The work will include research within small molecule NMR spectroscopy. Requirements A doctoral degree, or a foreign degree equivalent to a doctoral degree, in chemistry, physics, biology, or a related field, or other qualifications assessed by the employer as equivalent. Extensive knowledge of and practical experience with solution-state NMR spectroscopy. In ranking eligible candidates special importance will be given to scientific skills. Experience with full relaxation matrix analysis and the quantitative analysis of NOESY spectra is a requirement. Candidates must be able to express themselves well in spoken as well as written English. We attach great importance to personal qualities such as accuracy, creativity, openness, motivation, genuine scientific interest and social competence. It is important to us that our labs and our instruments are organized, clean and in good order, and you are expected to be a role model in this regard. You must have the ability to work well organized and structured. Since you will be involved in supporting the work of younger researchers, you need to be able to support individuals and ensure that the work environment is productive and pleasant. Qualifications desired Experience with organic synthesis and paramagnetic NMR will be considered an advantage. About the employment The employment is a temporary position of 2 years according to central collective agreement. Full time position. Starting date as agreed. Placement: Uppsala For further information about the position, please contact: Professor, Mate Erdelyi, mate.erdelyi@kemi.uu.se, +46 72 9999166. Please submit your application by 16 November 2026, UFV-PA 2026/3174 . Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Disciplinary Domain of Science and Technology, Faculty of Chemistry, Department of Chemistry - BMC Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Temporary position Pay: Individuell lönesättning Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/3174 Last application date: 16 November 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=983023": {
      "title": "Researcher",
      "description": "Researcher - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Researcher 2026-10-23 Would you like to develop AI-based methods to understand and predict recovery after traumatic brain injury? We welcome applications for a researcher position at Uppsala University. The Department of Medical Sciences is a large clinical institution with more than 250 employees and over 900 additional coworkers connected via the Uppsala University Hospital. The Department of Medical Sciences has a broad research profile with strong research groups in a number of different areas. The research carried out at the department is performed in close connection with the clinical activities at the Uppsala University Hospital, which includes both basic studies on the causes of a variety of illnesses and the development and evaluation of improved diagnostics and new treatment methods. More information about the Department of Medical Sciences can be found at https://www.uu.se/en/department/medical-sciences . The neurotrauma research group at Uppsala University and Uppsala University Hospital conducts clinical and translational research focusing on individual differences in recovery following traumatic brain injury. Our research combines clinical patient data, continuous physiological monitoring from neurocritical care, neuroimaging and advanced data analytics. This project aims to develop and validate AI-based models for dynamic outcome prediction and improved understanding of secondary brain injury, with the long-term goal of supporting personalised care. Duties The position involves developing, implementing and evaluating machine learning and artificial intelligence methods for research data from patients with traumatic brain injury (TBI). Main duties include: Processing and integrating longitudinal clinical data, physiological time series (e.g. ICP, CPP and blood pressure), laboratory data and imaging-derived variables. Developing and externally validating predictive models of clinical outcomes and physiological changes during intensive care. Developing reproducible analytical pipelines, quality assurance, documentation and secure data workflows. Conducting scientific analyses, preparing manuscripts and presenting findings in interdisciplinary collaboration with clinicians and researchers. Requirements PhD in computer science, artificial intelligence, machine learning, bioinformatics or another field relevant to the position. Documented experience developing and evaluating machine learning or deep learning models. Strong Python programming skills and experience with relevant machine learning frameworks, such as PyTorch. Experience in quantitative data analysis and scientific research, including the ability to document and communicate results. Ability to work independently and in interdisciplinary teams, and excellent English communication skills. Additional qualifications Experience in generative artificial intelligence, including diffusion models, synthetic data generation and data augmentation techniques. ⁠Experience in high-performance computing (HPC), GPU acceleration, and the development and optimization of scalable machine learning and deep learning workflows. Experience in computer vision, medical or scientific image analysis, and multimodal machine learning involving heterogeneous data sources. About the employment The employment is 12 months . Scope: full-time . Starting date: as agreed. Placement: Uppsala . For further information about the position, please contact: Elham Rostami, elham.rostami@uu.se . In this recruitment we have replaced the cover letter with questions that you are asked to answer when making your application. The answers will be used as a part of the selection process. Please submit your application by November 9, 2026 , UFV-PA 2026/3235. Are you considering moving to Sweden to work at Uppsala University? Find out more about what it´s like to work and live in Sweden. Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Department of Medical Sciences Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Temporary position Pay: Individual salary Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/3235 Last application date: 9 November 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=978180": {
      "title": "Postdoc position in quantum matter theory with specialization in unconventional superconductivity",
      "description": "Postdoc position in quantum matter theory with specialization in unconventional superconductivity - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Postdoc position in quantum matter theory with specialization in unconventional superconductivity 2026-10-22 The research conducted at the Department of Physics and Astronomy encompasses a wide range of physics topics, distributed over nine divisions. The department is located in the Ångström laboratory and employs nearly 400 people, 100 of whom are doctoral students. It offers a broad physics curriculum to undergraduate and graduate students, participation in nationally and internationally leading projects for researchers, and opportunities for partnership with industry and various outreach activities. Read more on www.uu.se/physics The position is within the Quantum Matter Theory research program, with research focusing on theory of quantum condensed matter, where quantum mechanical effects in a prominent way determine the properties. The research activities span many contemporary parts of physics, such as unconventional superconductivity, topological matter, non-equilibrium phenomena in nanosystems, strongly correlated systems, and quantum information. The project will be carried out in the research group of Prof. Annica Black-Schaffer, currently consisting of 15 Ph.D. students and postdocs. For more information, please visit the group webpage: https://materials-theory.physics.uu.se/black-schaffer/ Research area and duties: We are looking for an ambitious and motivated postdoc in quantum matter theory for work combining unconventional superconductivity and quantum geometry. The work will involve both numerical simulations and analytical work. The postdoc candidate is expected work both independently and in collaboration with other group members and external collaborators. Requirements: Ph.D. degree in physics or closely related subject. The Ph.D. degree must have been obtained at the start of the employment and no more than three years prior to the application deadline, however, periods of e.g. parental or sick leave may be deducted from this three-year period. The applicant should have a strong research background in theory of unconventional superconductivity and quantum geometry applied to condensed matter systems. Fluency in both written and spoken English is a requirement. Additional qualifications: We are searching for a postdoc candidate how is responsible, self-motivated, and has demonstrated independence in research, and at the same time works well in a research group. Emphasis will be therefore be placed on personal abilities, including independence, motivation, as well good organizational and collaborative skills. Emphasis will also be placed on the ability to publish scientific work in high-quality journals and to give presentations at scientific meetings. A combination of analytical and numerical skills is advantageous. Pervious postdoc experience is advantageous. Previous experience working on quantum geometric aspects of superconductors is also advantageous. About the application In addition to your CV, please include a publication list and a research statement with your application. In this recruitment we have replaced the cover letter with questions that you are asked to answer when making your application. The answers will be used as a part of the selection process. About the employment: The employment is a temporary position of two years, with a possibility of a one-year extension, according to central collective agreement. Scope of employment 100 %. Starting date: 1 May 2027 or upon agreement. Placement: Uppsala. For more information please contact Prof. Annica Black-Schaffer, annica.black-schaffer@physics.uu.se, phone +46 (0)76-795 06 49. Please submit your application by November 20 2026, UFV-PA 2026/3056 Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Department of Physics and Astronomy Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Temporary position Pay: Månadslön Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/3056 Last application date: 20 November 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
