    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=980532": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral position in fast-neutron dosimetry and reference neutron fields",
      "description": "Postdoctoral position in fast-neutron dosimetry and reference neutron fields - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Postdoctoral position in fast-neutron dosimetry and reference neutron fields 2026-10-20 Are you interested in working with fast neutrons, neutron dosimetry and detector characterisation, with the support of competent and friendly colleagues in an international environment? Are you looking for an employer that invests in sustainable employeeship and offers safe, favourable working conditions? We welcome you to apply for a postdoc position at Uppsala University. The Department of Physics and Astronomy is located in the Ångström Laboratory and employs nearly 400 people, around 100 of whom are doctoral students. It offers a broad physics curriculum to undergraduate and graduate students, participation in nationally and internationally leading projects for researchers, and opportunities for partnership with industry and various outreach activities. Read more on uu.se/physics. The position is placed at the Division of Applied Nuclear Physics. We connect fundamental nuclear physics research with applications in nuclear technology and radiation safety. Examples of our research areas are experimental studies of nuclear fission, neutron spectrometry for plasma diagnostics in fusion, nuclear data evaluation methodology, and technical aspects of nuclear safeguards and disarmament. The division operates NESSA, a 14 MeV neutron facility in the FREIA hall at the Ångström Laboratory. Since November 2025, NESSA has been equipped with a D-T neutron generator delivering up to 10⁸ neutrons per second, making it a unique facility in Sweden and the Nordic region. The position is funded by the Swedish Radiation Safety Authority (SSM) within the project “A Reference Neutron Field at Uppsala for Detector Response, Dosimetry and Cross-Calibration in Support of Radiation Protection and Preparedness”. The project will establish and characterise a variable-energy reference neutron field at Uppsala, based on 14 MeV neutrons from NESSA and complemented by charged-particle-induced neutron fields at the Uppsala Tandem Laboratory, and link the measurements to the European metrology chain. The results will strengthen national competence in radiation protection and emergency preparedness. Duties You will carry the experimental and computational work of the project within the NESSA team, including: building and validating Monte Carlo models of the NESSA bunker and the detector systems using several codes, e.g. MCNP, FLUKA, Geant4, PHITS and FISPACT-II; commissioning and operating a detector suite consisting of, e.g., liquid scintillators with pulse-shape discrimination, micro fission chambers, and activation foils analysed by HPGe gamma-ray spectrometry; characterising the neutron fields in terms of energy spectra and fluence with full uncertainty budgets; performing shielding and moderation experiments (e.g. polyethylene and concrete) and benchmarking the results against simulations; measuring detector response functions in neutron fields at the Uppsala Tandem Laboratory; planning and carrying out a cross-calibration campaign at a reference neutron fields (e.g. PTB Braunschweig); publishing the results in peer-reviewed journals and international conferences; contributing to education and training in neutron measurement techniques for students and for staff from authorities and industry. We also encourage you to develop your own research profile and to contribute to applications that help develop the activities of the division. Requirements PhD degree in physics or a related field, or a foreign degree equivalent to a PhD degree in physics or a related field. The degree needs to be obtained by the time of the decision of employment. Priority will be given to applicants who have completed their degree no more than three years before the deadline for applications. Due to special circumstances, the degree may have been obtained earlier. The three-year period can be extended due to circumstances such as sick leave, parental leave, duties in labour unions, etc. You must have documented experience in experimental nuclear or radiation physics, for example neutron measurements, radiation detectors or dosimetry, as well as experience in Monte Carlo simulation of radiation transport. Very good communication skills in spoken and written English are required. We are looking for someone who is structured and thorough, who can work independently and drive an experimental project forward, and who collaborates well with others. Additional qualifications The qualifications listed below are meant to help you point out relevant experience and expertise. We strongly encourage you to apply even if your experience does not match all of them: Experience in experimental techniques using fast neutrons. Experience with liquid scintillators and pulse-shape discrimination, fission chambers, or digital data acquisition. Experience in neutron spectrometry and neutron dosimetry, e.g. Bonner sphere spectrometry and spectrum unfolding methods. Experience with neutron activation techniques and HPGe gamma-ray spectrometry. Proficiency in one or more of the codes MCNP, FLUKA, Geant4, PHITS and FISPACT-II. Experience in uncertainty analysis and metrology. Experience with experiments at accelerators or other neutron sources. About the employment The employment is a temporary position of two years according to central collective agreement. Full time position. Starting date 1 February 2027 or as agreed. Placement: Ångström Laboratory, Uppsala. For further information about the position, please contact: Stephan Pomp, +46-70-167 9003, stephan.pomp@physics.uu.se. In this recruitment we have replaced the cover letter with questions that you are asked to answer when making your application. The answers will be used as a part of the selection process. Please submit your application by 7 December 2026, UFV-PA 2026/3137. Are you considering moving to Sweden to work at Uppsala University? Find out more about what it´s like to work and live in Sweden . Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Department of Physics and Astronomy Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Temporary position Pay: Individual salary setting Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/3137 Last application date: 7 December 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=980644": {
      "title": "Redaktör till tidskriften EID",
      "description": "Redaktör till tidskriften EID - Uppsala University Use of cookies Uppsala University uses cookies to make your website experience better. Read more about cookies Accept all cookies Accept only necessary cookies Customize settings Skip to main content uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Redaktör till tidskriften EID Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Redaktör till tidskriften EID This job advertisement is only available in Swedish . HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PI