    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=979632": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral position in Biopharmaceuticals",
      "description": "Postdoctoral position in Biopharmaceuticals - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Postdoctoral position in Biopharmaceuticals 2026-10-19 The Department of Pharmacy at Uppsala University has an interdisciplinary environment at the center of the pharmaceutical arena. With frontline research, first-rate education and extensive collaborations we constitute a driving force in the development of our academic field. In this inspiring environment our rich diversity of research groups, several of international prominence, develop and conduct work of great scientific importance. Among our core competencies are computational modelling and simulations, PKPD, in vitro ADME models, advanced in vivo methods, biological medicines, as well as patient and societal aspects, from optimising the use of drugs in individuals to societal pharmaceutical policies. Together, we form a unique cluster of academic competencies within pharmaceutical science, playing a key role in shaping the future of pharmacy in both Sweden and globally. Our scientific focus areas include: Pharmacokinetics & Pharmacodynamics • Pharmacometrics • Clinical Pharmacy • Advanced Drug Delivery • Molecular Pharmaceutics • Biological Drugs • Pharmacoepidemiology • Social Pharmacy More information www.farmaci.uu.se Duties: The position is focused on the development of AAV-based therapies for Alzheimer’s disease and other neurodegenerative disorders. The work will involve the design, production, and characterization of AAV vectors, as well as the evaluation of therapeutic strategies in vitro and in vivo . The research group develops biologic therapies for neurodegenerative diseases, primarily Alzheimer’s disease and Parkinson’s disease. We work with several therapeutic modalities, including protein- and antibody-based drugs as well as AAV-based gene therapy. The exact duties may be adapted to some extent based on the candidate’s skills and experience; however, the design and production of biopharmaceuticals and in vivo experiments will be central components of the position. Some teaching and administrative duties may also be included. Qualifications: We are seeking a candidate with a PhD in a field relevant to the position, such as molecular biology, biotechnology , gene therapy, neuroscience , or a related discipline. The degree needs to be obtained by the time of the decision of employment. Priority will be given to applicants who have completed their degree no more than three years before the deadline for applications. Due to special circumstances, the degree may have been obtained earlier. The three-year period can be extended due to circumstances such as sick leave, parental leave, duties in labour unions, etc. Applicants must have experience in experimental work within molecular biology, gene therapy, biologics, or a related field. As in vivo studies constitute an important part of the projects, candidates must be willing to work with animal experiments. Merits and Preferred Qualifications: Particularly valuable experience includes: Design and optimization of AAV vectors Production, purification, and characterization of AAVs Molecular cloning and construction of expression vectors Development of gene therapy-based strategies AAV and protein purification, for example using ÄKTA systems Sterile cell culture techniques and cultivation of various cell types Additional merit will be given for experience in: ELISA and flow cytometry/FACS In vivo experiments Neurodegenerative diseases Teaching We are looking for a curious, creative, and motivated individual with a strong interest in developing novel therapeutic strategies. You should be able to work independently, take initiative, and collaborate effectively with others. Great importance is placed on communication and teamwork skills, as well as a willingness to contribute to an open, supportive, and positive working environment within the research group. About the employment The employment is a temporary position of 2 years according to central collective agreement. Full time position. Starting date 2027-02-01 or as agreed. Placement: Uppsala For further information about the position, please contact: Professor Greta Hultqvist, greta.hultqvist@uu.se In this recruitment we have replaced the cover letter with questions that you are asked to answer when making your application. The answers will be used as a part of the selection process. Please submit your application by 16 November 2026 , UFV-PA 2026 /3107. Are you considering moving to Sweden to work at Uppsala University? Find out more about what it´s like to work and live in Sweden. Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Department of Pharmacy Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Temporary position Pay: Individuell lönesättning Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/3107 Last application date: 16 November 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    },
