    "https://www.uu.se/en/about-uu/join-us/jobs-and-vacancies/job-details?query=979403": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral researcher in Infectious Diseases, with a focus on in vitro and in silico Bacteriology",
      "description": "Postdoctoral researcher in Infectious Diseases, with a focus on in vitro and in silico Bacteriology - Uppsala University uu.se Students Staff Alumni uu.se Search Search. Search suggestions are presented below the search box. Search Search courses and programmes Svenska Menu Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Pages for: Students Staff Alumni Go directly to: Library Press News Events Support Uppsala University Uppsala University About the University Join us Jobs and vacancies Job details Study Research Collaboration and innovation About the University Vision, goals and strategies Structure and governance The University area Academic traditions History Cultural heritage Join us Contact and organisation Postdoctoral researcher in Infectious Diseases, with a focus on in vitro and in silico Bacteriology 2026-10-14 Are you interested in working with microbiology, with the support of competent and friendly colleagues in an international environment? Are you looking for an employer that invests in sustainable employeeship and offers safe, favourable working conditions? We welcome you to apply for a postdoctoral position at Uppsala University. The Department of Medical Sciences is a large clinical institution with approximately 250 employees and over 300 individuals affiliated with Uppsala University Hospital. The department has a broad research profile with strong research groups in various areas. Research takes place in close connection to clinical activities at Uppsala University Hospital and encompasses both fundamental studies on the causes of diseases and the development and evaluation of improved diagnostics and new treatment methods. More information about the department's activities can be found at: https://www.uu.se/en/department/medical-sciences . Job Responsibilities We are seeking a highly motivated postdoctoral researcher with a strong interest in microbiology and infectious diseases. The focus will be on projects related to bacterial genomics and phylogeny as well as antibiotic resistance. The work involves practical microbiological laboratory work ('wet lab') as well as a significant portion of bioinformatic analysis, such as sequence data analysis. You will be involved in several projects within the research group, taking on a coordinating role in addition to subject expertise. Several projects will address the intersection of humans, animals, and the environment. The research group conducts both clinical studies and basic research. As a postdoctoral researcher, you will work with a team of diverse scientific backgrounds and interact with and supervise students in the group. Requirements You should have a PhD degree in microbiology with a focus on bacteriological research and antibiotic resistance. The degree needs to be obtained by the time of the decision of employment. Those who have obtained a PhD degree three years prior to the application deadline are primarily considered for employment. The starting point of the three-year frame period is the application deadline. The ability to work independently and a strong interest in translational microbiology are essential. Documented competence in bacteriological lab work, including method development and experimental design, with bacteria and genomic analysis (including AMR) is required. Teaching and/or supervision experience is required. Fluent spoken and written English is necessary, and the ability to communicate in both spoken and written Swedish is also required. Additional qualifications A background in veterinary medicine and infection biology is meriting. Experience using Nanopore sequencing and bacterial genomic analysis using the software CLC are merits of interest, as well as experience in genetic engineering of bacterial isolates and interdisciplinary collaboration. Documents to be attached to your application: CV List of publications Letter of recommendation About the Employment The employment is a temporary position of 2 years according to central collective agreement. Full-time position. Starting date as soon as possible or as agreed. Location: Uppsala. For more information about the position, please contact: Josef Järhult, josef.jarhult@medsci.uu.se . Welcome with your application no later than November 11 2026, UFV-PA 2026/3100. Uppsala University is a broad research university with a strong international position. The ultimate goal is to conduct education and research of the highest quality and relevance to make a difference in society. Our most important asset is all of our 7,500 employees and 53,000 students who, with curiosity and commitment, make Uppsala University one of Sweden’s most exciting workplaces. Read more about our benefits and what it is like to work at Uppsala University https://uu.se/om-uu/jobba-hos-oss/ The position may be subject to security vetting. If security vetting is conducted, the applicant must pass the vetting process to be eligible for employment. Please do not send offers of recruitment or advertising services. Submit your application through Uppsala University's recruitment system. Employee organizations: Saco-S - saco-s@uu.se, Seko - seko@uadm.uu.se, ST (OFR/S) - ofr@uu.se Placement: Uppsala University Faculty of Medicine, Department of Medical Sciences Scope: Full time Working hours: 100% Type of employment: Temporary position Pay: Individuell lönesättning Number of positions: 1 Town: Uppsala Union representative: Number of reference: UFV-PA 2026/3100 Last application date: 11 November 2026 Apply for position HR Excellence in Research Uppsala University has received the European Commission acknowledgement HR Excellence in Research, an award that indicates that Uppsala University is an employer with a stimulating and favourable working environment. Find out more about HR Excellence in Research Contact +46 18 471 00 00 (switchboard) Contact the University Visit us Departments & units Campuses Museums & gardens Map of Uppsala University Wifi for visitors Shortcuts Vice-Chancellor’s Blog Giftshop online Press & media Jobs & vacancies University management Support Uppsala University International Faculty and Staff Services Staff Gateway Current procurements Whistleblowing function Follow Uppsala University on © Uppsala University Tel: +46 18 471 00 00 P.O. Box 256, SE-751 05 Uppsala, SWEDEN Registration number: 202100-2932 VAT number: SE202100293201 PIC: 999985029 Registrar About this website Manage cookies Privacy policy Editor: kommunikation@uu.se"
    }
